sha":"d94f3c63f36c21222def96c12f62997ebd8a5fa8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DJJones66/BrainDrive-Chat-With-Docs-Plugin/commits/d94f3c63f36c21222def96c12f62997ebd8a5fa8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47065940?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bekmuradov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bekmuradov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bekmuradov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bekmuradov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bekmuradov","id":47065940,"login":"bekmuradov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDY1OTQw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bekmuradov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bekmuradov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bekmuradov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bekmuradov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bekmuradov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bekmuradov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DJJones66/BrainDrive-Chat-With-Docs-Plugin/commits/46a5318dcb70163549e3cfd5b5236f4997a1074d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-11-13T14:46:14Z","email":"47065940+bekmuradov@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Beck Bekmyradov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-11-13T14:46:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: Phase 6 - ConversationManager, dead code cleanup, GreetingService (#32)\n\n* refactor: apply SRP to DataRepository, split into specialized repositories\n\n- Create infrastructure layer with HttpClient abstraction\n- Split DataRepository into 4 single-responsibility repositories:\n  - CollectionRepository: collections I/O\n  - DocumentRepository: documents I/O\n  - ChatSessionRepository: chat sessions/messages I/O\n  - RAGRepository: RAG search I/O\n- Keep DataRepository as facade for backward compatibility\n- Add comprehensive unit tests (16 tests, all passing)\n- Fix jest config: setupTests.ts path\n\nBenefits:\n- Each repository has single reason to change (SRP)\n- HttpClient provides anti-corruption layer for BrainDrive API\n- Repositories are easily testable without React\n- Clear separation of concerns\n- Non-breaking change\n\n* docs: add comprehensive refactoring plan with 11 phases\n\n* refactor: extract model config loading domain logic (Phase 3)\n\n- Create domain/models layer with SRP:\n  - ProviderResolver: map provider names to settings IDs\n  - ModelMapper: transform API responses to ModelInfo\n  - ModelConfigLoader: orchestrate model loading with Ollama fallback\n  - FallbackModelSelector: select default/fallback models\n- Add 34 passing unit tests for domain logic\n- Update CollectionChatViewShell: reduce from 160 to 55 lines (-105 lines)\n- Update EvaluationViewShell: reduce from 45 to 25 lines (-20 lines)\n- Centralize duplicate model loading logic from 3 components\n\nBenefits:\n- Eliminates ~200+ lines of duplicate code\n- Pure domain logic is easily testable\n- Single source of truth for model configuration\n- Components delegate to domain services\n\n* docs: mark Phase 3 complete in refactoring plan\n\n* chore: remove dead code (3676 lines)\n\n- Delete ChatView.tsx (1122 lines, 100% commented)\n- Delete CollectionChatView.tsx (2554 lines, 100% commented)\n\nTotal reduction: -3676 lines of unmaintained code\n\n* docs: update Phase 5 with detailed CollectionChatViewShell analysis\n\n- Add analysis findings: 2514 lines, 900-1000 extractable\n- Break Phase 5 into 6 priorities with line counts\n- Priority 1: ConversationRepository/Loader (200+ lines)\n- Priority 2: StreamingChatHandler (300+ lines)\n- Priority 3: PersonaResolver (130+ lines)\n- Priority 4: DocumentUploadHandler (90+ lines)\n- Priority 5: PageSettingsService (60+ lines)\n- Priority 6: ScrollStateManager (265 lines) - service class, not hook\n- Note: Plugin requires class components (host system constraint)\n- Target: Reduce component from 2514 to ~1300-1600 lines\n\n* refactor: extract user and conversation repositories (Phase 5)\n\n- Create UserRepository for user data operations (44 lines, 5 tests)\n- Create ConversationRepository for conversation data operations (143 lines, 20 tests)\n- Extract fetchConversations, refreshConversationsList logic\n- Extract conversation sorting (sortByRecency, getSortTimestamp)\n- Reduce CollectionChatViewShell by 154 lines (202 lines removed)\n- Add jest test commands: test, test:watch, test:domain, test:infrastructure, test:coverage\n- All 54 domain tests passing\n\n* refactor: extract StreamingChatHandler (Phase 5.2)\n\n- Create StreamingChatHandler for streaming AI request lifecycle (115 lines)\n- Single Responsibility: Orchestrate streaming with abort control\n- Manages AbortController lifecycle and AI service calls\n- Add 20 comprehensive tests (100% coverage)\n- All 74 domain tests passing\n- Update refactoring plan with completed items\n\n* docs: add host system documentation\n\n- Add plugin naming conventions guide\n- Add plugin theming guide (light/dark mode)\n- Add theming implementation details\n- Reference docs for plugin development\n\n* refactor: extract ChatScrollManager and ModelKeyHelper (Phase 5.3)\n\nExtract scroll management into reusable service:\n- ChatScrollManager: 399 lines, 36 tests\n- ModelKeyHelper utility: 33 lines, 10 tests\n\nScroll Manager Features:\n- Smart auto-scroll with user intent tracking\n- Anchor offset (prevents hiding content)\n- Debounced scroll for performance\n- State machine for scroll indicators\n- Configurable thresholds and grace periods\n\nRemoved from CollectionChatViewShell:\n- 265 lines of scroll logic\n- 9 instance variables\n- 10 private methods\n\nBenefits:\n- Single Responsibility: UI scroll state isolated\n- Testability: 36 unit tests for scroll behavior\n- Reusability: Can be used in EvaluationViewShell\n- Maintainability: Clear separation of concerns\n\nTest Results:\n- All 136 tests passing\n- ChatScrollManager: 36/36 tests pass\n- ModelKeyHelper: 10/10 tests pass\n\nImpact:\n- CollectionChatViewShell: 2,410 → 2,176 lines (234 lines removed)\n- Test coverage: +46 tests\n- Zero breaking changes\n\nRelated: Phase 5 refactoring plan\n\n* refactor: extract ConversationLoader (Phase 5.4)\n\nExtract conversation loading into reusable service:\n- ConversationLoader: 320 lines, 28 tests\n- Handles conversation history, persona, and model loading\n\nConversation Loader Features:\n- Load conversation messages from API\n- Load conversation with persona/model metadata\n- Resolve model and persona from conversation data\n- Update conversation persona\n- Clean message content (normalize, remove legacy context)\n\nRemoved from CollectionChatViewShell:\n- 213 lines of conversation loading logic\n- cleanMessageContent, loadConversationHistory, loadConversationWithPersona, updateConversationPersona\n\nBenefits:\n- Single Responsibility: Conversation data loading isolated\n- Testability: 28 unit tests for loading logic\n- Reusability: Can be used in other conversation views\n- Maintainability: Clear separation of data access\n\nImpact:\n- CollectionChatViewShell: 2,176 → 2,044 lines (132 lines removed)\n- Test coverage: +28 tests (164 total passing)\n- Uses ModelKeyHelper for key generation\n\n* refactor: extract PersonaResolver (Phase 5.5)\n\nExtract persona management into reusable service:\n- PersonaResolver: 220 lines, 23 tests\n- Handles persona loading, resolution, and deduplication\n\nPersonaResolver Features:\n- Load personas from API or use provided personas\n- Resolve pending persona IDs to PersonaInfo objects\n- Fetch individual personas by ID\n- Prevent duplicate API requests\n- Automatic deduplication of personas\n\nRemoved from CollectionChatViewShell:\n- 100 lines of persona management logic\n- loadPersonas implementation\n- fetchPersonaById implementation\n- resolvePendingPersonaSelection implementation\n- pendingPersonaRequestId tracking\n\nBenefits:\n- Single Responsibility: Persona management isolated\n- Testability: 23 unit tests for persona logic\n- Reusability: Can be used in persona selection components\n- Maintainability: Clear separation of concerns\n\nImpact:\n- CollectionChatViewShell: 2,044 → 1,978 lines (66 lines removed)\n- Test coverage: +23 tests (187 total passing)\n- Zero breaking changes\n\n* refactor: extract PageSettingsService (Phase 5.6)\n\nExtract page settings and page context logic into dedicated service\n\n- Create PageSettingsService with 136 lines, 31 tests\n- Manages page-specific settings with global fallbacks\n- Handles page context subscriptions and cleanup\n- Integrate into CollectionChatViewShell, removing 60 lines\n- Fix ChatScrollManager test timing (manual scroll unlock)\n\nAll 218 tests passing\n\n* refactor: use PersonaResolver in EvaluationViewShell\n\nReplace direct API call with PersonaResolver service for consistency\n\n- Remove duplicate persona loading logic\n- Delegate to PersonaResolver.loadPersonas()\n- Consistent with CollectionChatViewShell implementation\n- Already using ModelConfigLoader and FallbackModelSelector\n\nAll 218 tests passing\n\n* fix: use shared PersonaInfo type for build compatibility\n\nFix webpack build errors by using shared types\n\n- Use PersonaInfo from src/types.ts in PersonaResolver\n- Use PersonaInfo from src/types.ts in ConversationLoader\n- Add ModelKeyHelper import to CollectionChatViewShell\n- Exclude test files from production build (tsconfig, webpack)\n\nBuild now succeeds with 218 tests passing\n\n* docs: add comprehensive AI agent refactoring instructions\n\nGuide for continuing Phase 6 refactoring of CollectionChatViewShell\n\n- TDD workflow with step-by-step process\n- Priority queue for 5 extractions (~490 lines)\n- Code patterns and testing examples\n- Success criteria and progress tracking\n- Common issues and solutions\n\nTarget: Reduce component from 2050 to under 1500 lines\n\n* refactor: extract ConversationManager (Phase 6.1)\n\nExtract conversation CRUD operations from CollectionChatViewShell:\n- handleConversationSelect\n- handleRenameConversation\n- handleShareConversation\n- handleDeleteConversation\n- toggleConversationMenu\n\nBenefits:\n- Reduced CollectionChatViewShell from 2050 to 1983 lines (-67 lines)\n- 20 test cases added (238 total tests passing)\n- TDD approach with service delegation pattern\n- Returns state updates instead of mutating\n- Dependency injection for api, addMessageToChat, loadConversationWithPersona\n\n* chore: delete dead code (2,858 lines removed)\n\nPhase 1 cleanup - Remove completely unused/commented code:\n\nDead handler files (never instantiated):\n- ChatHistoryManager.ts (498 lines) - replaced by ConversationRepository/Loader\n- ChatMessageHandler.ts (308 lines) - operations moved inline\n- ChatDocumentHandler.ts (293 lines) - operations moved inline\n- ChatStateManager.ts (266 lines) - state managed by React component\n- ChatSearchHandler.ts (279 lines) - entirely commented out\n- handlers/index.ts (6 lines) - exported dead handlers\n\nCommented service files (abandoned refactoring):\n- ChatService.ts (1,247 lines) - duplicates domain services\n- CollectionChatService.ts (692 lines) - entirely commented out\n\nBackup/unused code:\n- CollectionChatViewShell copy.tsx (247 lines) - backup file\n- menuButtonRef (1 line) - never assigned or used\n- Duplicate model key methods (12 lines) - use ModelKeyHelper instead\n- Commented JSX (9 lines) - old chat input markup\n\nResults:\n- Total deleted: 2,858 lines\n- CollectionChatViewShell: 1983 → 1961 lines (-22 lines)\n- All 238 tests passing\n- Build succeeds\n- Zero functionality impact (all dead code)\n\n* refactor: extract GreetingService (Phase 6.2)\n\nConsolidate duplicate greeting logic into reusable service.\n\nDuplicate pattern appeared in 4 locations:\n- CollectionChatViewShell.tsx (2 instances)\n- ConversationManager.ts (2 instances)\n\nPattern consolidated:\n  const personaGreeting = showPersonaSelection && selectedPersona?.sample_greeting;\n  const greetingContent = personaGreeting || defaultGreeting;\n\nCreated GreetingService with 3 static methods:\n- getGreeting() - Get appropriate greeting (persona or default)\n- shouldUsePersonaGreeting() - Check if persona greeting applies\n- getEffectivePersona() - Get persona respecting toggle state\n\nBenefits:\n- Single source of truth for greeting logic\n- 15 comprehensive tests (253 total passing)\n- Easier to maintain and extend\n- Clear, self-documenting API\n- DRY principle applied\n\nFiles:\n- Created: src/domain/chat/GreetingService.ts (88 lines)\n- Created: src/domain/chat/__tests__/GreetingService.test.ts (168 lines)\n- Modified: CollectionChatViewShell.tsx (replaced 2 instances)\n- Modified: ConversationManager.ts (replaced 2 instances)\n\n* build: update dist after refactoring\n\nUpdate production build artifacts after:\n- ConversationManager extraction\n- Dead code removal (2,858 lines)\n- GreetingService extraction\n\nChanges:\n- dist/676.js → dist/84.js (chunk rename)\n- Updated main.js and remoteEntry.js","tree":{"sha":"3ed190d8f690bbd1268c82fd1057c020393811c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DJJones66/BrainDrive-Chat-With-Docs-Plugin/git/trees/3ed190d8f690bbd1268c82fd1057c020393811c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DJJones66/BrainDrive-Chat-With-Docs-Plugin/git/commits/46a5318dcb70163549e3cfd5b5236f4997a1074d","verification":{"payload":"tree 3ed190d8f690bbd1268c82fd1057c020393811c4\nparent 89ec9b6d9dfd194d7cb9fc17e04e3e9fffafba0d\nauthor Beck Bekmyradov <47065940+bekmuradov@users.noreply.github.com> 1763045174 +0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1763045174 +0400\n\nrefactor: Phase 6 - ConversationManager, dead code cleanup, GreetingService (#32)\n\n* refactor: apply SRP to DataRepository, split into specialized repositories\n\n- Create infrastructure layer with HttpClient abstraction\n- Split DataRepository into 4 single-responsibility repositories:\n  - CollectionRepository: collections I/O\n  - DocumentRepository: documents I/O\n  - ChatSessionRepository: chat sessions/messages I/O\n  - RAGRepository: RAG search I/O\n- Keep DataRepository as facade for backward compatibility\n- Add comprehensive unit tests (16 tests, all passing)\n- Fix jest config: setupTests.ts path\n\nBenefits:\n- Each repository has single reason to change (SRP)\n- HttpClient provides anti-corruption layer for BrainDrive API\n- Repositories are easily testable without React\n- Clear separation of concerns\n- Non-breaking change\n\n* docs: add comprehensive refactoring plan with 11 phases\n\n* refactor: extract model config loading domain logic (Phase 3)\n\n- Create domain/models layer with SRP:\n  - ProviderResolver: map provider names to settings IDs\n  - ModelMapper: transform API responses to ModelInfo\n  - ModelConfigLoader: orchestrate model loading with Ollama fallback\n  - FallbackModelSelector: select default/fallback models\n- Add 34 passing unit tests for domain logic\n- Update CollectionChatViewShell: reduce from 160 to 55 lines (-105 lines)\n- Update EvaluationViewShell: reduce from 45 to 25 lines (-20 lines)\n- Centralize duplicate model loading logic from 3 components\n\nBenefits:\n- Eliminates ~200+ lines of duplicate code\n- Pure domain logic is easily testable\n- Single source of truth for model configuration\n- Components delegate to domain services\n\n* docs: mark Phase 3 complete in refactoring plan\n\n* chore: remove dead code (3676 lines)\n\n- Delete ChatView.tsx (1122 lines, 100% commented)\n- Delete CollectionChatView.tsx (2554 lines, 100% commented)\n\nTotal reduction: -3676 lines of unmaintained code\n\n* docs: update Phase 5 with detailed CollectionChatViewShell analysis\n\n- Add analysis findings: 2514 lines, 900-1000 extractable\n- Break Phase 5 into 6 priorities with line counts\n- Priority 1: ConversationRepository/Loader (200+ lines)\n- Priority 2: StreamingChatHandler (300+ lines)\n- Priority 3: PersonaResolver (130+ lines)\n- Priority 4: DocumentUploadHandler (90+ lines)\n- Priority 5: PageSettingsService (60+ lines)\n- Priority 6: ScrollStateManager (265 lines) - service class, not hook\n- Note: Plugin requires class components (host system constraint)\n- Target: Reduce component from 2514 to ~1300-1600 lines\n\n* refactor: extract user and conversation repositories (Phase 5)\n\n- Create UserRepository for user data operations (44 lines, 5 tests)\n- Create ConversationRepository for conversation data operations (143 lines, 20 tests)\n- Extract fetchConversations, refreshConversationsList logic\n- Extract conversation sorting (sortByRecency, getSortTimestamp)\n- Reduce CollectionChatViewShell by 154 lines (202 lines removed)\n- Add jest test commands: test, test:watch, test:domain, test:infrastructure, test:coverage\n- All 54 domain tests passing\n\n* refactor: extract StreamingChatHandler (Phase 5.2)\n\n- Create StreamingChatHandler for streaming AI request lifecycle (115 lines)\n- Single Responsibility: Orchestrate streaming with abort control\n- Manages AbortController lifecycle and AI service calls\n- Add 20 comprehensive tests (100% coverage)\n- All 74 domain tests passing\n- Update refactoring plan with completed items\n\n* docs: add host system documentation\n\n- Add plugin naming conventions guide\n- Add plugin theming guide (light/dark mode)\n- Add theming implementation details\n- Reference docs for plugin development\n\n* refactor: extract ChatScrollManager and ModelKeyHelper (Phase 5.3)\n\nExtract scroll management into reusable service:\n- ChatScrollManager: 399 lines, 36 tests\n- ModelKeyHelper utility: 33 lines, 10 tests\n\nScroll Manager Features:\n- Smart auto-scroll with user intent tracking\n- Anchor offset (prevents hiding content)\n- Debounced scroll for performance\n- State machine for scroll indicators\n- Configurable thresholds and grace periods\n\nRemoved from CollectionChatViewShell:\n- 265 lines of scroll logic\n- 9 instance variables\n- 10 private methods\n\nBenefits:\n- Single Responsibility: UI scroll state isolated\n- Testability: 36 unit tests for scroll behavior\n- Reusability: Can be used in EvaluationViewShell\n- Maintainability: Clear separation of concerns\n\nTest Results:\n- All 136 tests passing\n- ChatScrollManager: 36/36 tests pass\n- ModelKeyHelper: 10/10 tests pass\n\nImpact:\n- CollectionChatViewShell: 2,410 → 2,176 lines (234 lines removed)\n- Test coverage: +46 tests\n- Zero breaking changes\n\nRelated: Phase 5 refactoring plan\n\n* refactor: extract ConversationLoader (Phase 5.4)\n\nExtract conversation loading into reusable service:\n- ConversationLoader: 320 lines, 28 tests\n- Handles conversation history, persona, and model loading\n\nConversation Loader Features:\n- Load conversation messages from API\n- Load conversation with persona/model metadata\n- Resolve model and persona from conversation data\n- Update conversation persona\n- Clean message content (normalize, remove legacy context)\n\nRemoved from CollectionChatViewShell:\n- 213 lines of conversation loading logic\n- cleanMessageContent, loadConversationHistory, loadConversationWithPersona, updateConversationPersona\n\nBenefits:\n- Single Responsibility: Conversation data loading isolated\n- Testability: 28 unit tests for loading logic\n- Reusability: Can be used in other conversation views\n- Maintainability: Clear separation of data access\n\nImpact:\n- CollectionChatViewShell: 2,176 → 2,044 lines (132 lines removed)\n- Test coverage: +28 tests (164 total passing)\n- Uses ModelKeyHelper for key generation\n\n* refactor: extract PersonaResolver (Phase 5.5)\n\nExtract persona management into reusable service:\n- PersonaResolver: 220 lines, 23 tests\n- Handles persona loading, resolution, and deduplication\n\nPersonaResolver Features:\n- Load personas from API or use provided personas\n- Resolve pending persona IDs to PersonaInfo objects\n- Fetch individual personas by ID\n- Prevent duplicate API requests\n- Automatic deduplication of personas\n\nRemoved from CollectionChatViewShell:\n- 100 lines of persona management logic\n- loadPersonas implementation\n- fetchPersonaById implementation\n- resolvePendingPersonaSelection implementation\n- pendingPersonaRequestId tracking\n\nBenefits:\n- Single Responsibility: Persona management isolated\n- Testability: 23 unit tests for persona logic\n- Reusability: Can be used in persona selection components\n- Maintainability: Clear separation of concerns\n\nImpact:\n- CollectionChatViewShell: 2,044 → 1,978 lines (66 lines removed)\n- Test coverage: +23 tests (187 total passing)\n- Zero breaking changes\n\n* refactor: extract PageSettingsService (Phase 5.6)\n\nExtract page settings and page context logic into dedicated service\n\n- Create PageSettingsService with 136 lines, 31 tests\n- Manages page-specific settings with global fallbacks\n- Handles page context subscriptions and cleanup\n- Integrate into CollectionChatViewShell, removing 60 lines\n- Fix ChatScrollManager test timing (manual scroll unlock)\n\nAll 218 tests passing\n\n* refactor: use PersonaResolver in EvaluationViewShell\n\nReplace direct API call with PersonaResolver service for consistency\n\n- Remove duplicate persona loading logic\n- Delegate to PersonaResolver.loadPersonas()\n- Consistent with CollectionChatViewShell implementation\n- Already using ModelConfigLoader and FallbackModelSelector\n\nAll 218 tests passing\n\n* fix: use shared PersonaInfo type for build compatibility\n\nFix webpack build errors by using shared types\n\n- Use PersonaInfo from src/types.ts in PersonaResolver\n- Use PersonaInfo from src/types.ts in ConversationLoader\n- Add ModelKeyHelper import to CollectionChatViewShell\n- Exclude test files from production build (tsconfig, webpack)\n\nBuild now succeeds with 218 tests passing\n\n* docs: add comprehensive AI agent refactoring instructions\n\nGuide for continuing Phase 6 refactoring of CollectionChatViewShell\n\n- TDD workflow with step-by-step process\n- Priority queue for 5 extractions (~490 lines)\n- Code patterns and testing examples\n- Success criteria and progress tracking\n- Common issues and solutions\n\nTarget: Reduce component from 2050 to under 1500 lines\n\n* refactor: extract ConversationManager (Phase 6.1)\n\nExtract conversation CRUD operations from CollectionChatViewShell:\n- handleConversationSelect\n- handleRenameConversation\n- handleShareConversation\n- handleDeleteConversation\n- toggleConversationMenu\n\nBenefits:\n- Reduced CollectionChatViewShell from 2050 to 1983 lines (-67 lines)\n- 20 test cases added (238 total tests passing)\n- TDD approach with service delegation pattern\n- Returns state updates instead of mutating\n- Dependency injection for api, addMessageToChat, loadConversationWithPersona\n\n* chore: delete dead code (2,858 lines removed)\n\nPhase 1 cleanup - Remove completely unused/commented code:\n\nDead handler files (never instantiated):\n- ChatHistoryManager.ts (498 lines) - replaced by ConversationRepository/Loader\n- ChatMessageHandler.ts (308 lines) - operations moved inline\n- ChatDocumentHandler.ts (293 lines) - operations moved inline\n- ChatStateManager.ts (266 lines) - state managed by React component\n- ChatSearchHandler.ts (279 lines) - entirely commented out\n- handlers/index.ts (6 lines) - exported dead handlers\n\nCommented service files (abandoned refactoring):\n- ChatService.ts (1,247 lines) - duplicates domain services\n- CollectionChatService.ts (692 lines) - entirely commented out\n\nBackup/unused code:\n- CollectionChatViewShell copy.tsx (247 lines) - backup file\n- menuButtonRef (1 line) - never assigned or used\n- Duplicate model key methods (12 lines) - use ModelKeyHelper instead\n- Commented JSX (9 lines) - old chat input markup\n\nResults:\n- Total deleted: 2,858 lines\n- CollectionChatViewShell: 1983 → 1961 lines (-22 lines)\n- All 238 tests passing\n- Build succeeds\n- Zero functionality impact (all dead code)\n\n* refactor: extract GreetingService (Phase 6.2)\n\nConsolidate duplicate greeting logic into reusable service.\n\nDuplicate pattern appeared in 4 locations:\n- CollectionChatViewShell.tsx (2 instances)\n- ConversationManager.ts (2 instances)\n\nPattern consolidated:\n  const personaGreeting = showPersonaSelection && selectedPersona?.sample_greeting;\n  const greetingContent = personaGreeting || defaultGreeting;\n\nCreated GreetingService with 3 static methods:\n- getGreeting() - Get appropriate greeting (persona or default)\n- shouldUsePersonaGreeting() - Check if persona greeting applies\n- getEffectivePersona() - Get persona respecting toggle state\n\nBenefits:\n- Single source of truth for greeting logic\n- 15 comprehensive tests (253 total passing)\n- Easier to maintain and extend\n- Clear, self-documenting API\n- DRY principle applied\n\nFiles:\n- Created: src/domain/chat/GreetingService.ts (88 lines)\n- Created: src/domain/chat/__tests__/GreetingService.test.ts (168 lines)\n- Modified: CollectionChatViewShell.tsx (replaced 2 instances)\n- Modified: ConversationManager.ts (replaced 2 instances)\n\n* build: update dist after refactoring\n\nUpdate production build artifacts after:\n- ConversationManager extraction\n- Dead code removal (2,858 lines)\n- GreetingService extraction\n\nChanges:\n- dist/676.js → dist/84.js (chunk rename)\n- Updated main.js and remoteEntry.js","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpFe82CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADhYQAHNhvW+wHupiUpQ5iV9jiO35\n/JCmDIwnXwCXBowLjX051PwM40jS9Q+a4Wk6ph1v0HDr4MD5MzffvB0uVp7WnkO/\n7PZwh24XorGfeXC/llbeQ+YJRRuxkgL47LbZQG1G9571SDwOhCEwUIxkVLwSYsNG\n8RVxnVCYubIm/e+3QDFe+IPyNH3xkn/5y5sf2qDNFXFORA3ajIiZjEGhuUaADp4M\nHPaZD26scF6/OdN8vtf7Kt2mCPMlyv9BlfOLtCQ8gozUU+zVWx+2PU8y9Ml8aUfa\nhzc2s0ZPTAyx6dCY3+QdzG/p5e3ohg/BnN6P8NfxbSXt4SOcpbWKdronGQ91SaAe\nmlBYVF3n88jTH053KZfxsfzEy8ZoiR8n31MvOnzOFsaUKqjFPNIC3cpO3p9wABCH\nSuSoHqHd7PMZ3f1JNfD+q18K7zxKg5SsJA