 for the `cql2elm` extension. Additionally, the web admin interface for extensions is improved for clarity, and dependencies are updated for easier extension management.","tree":{"sha":"ce32f068ae2b39cb3baa1850ca829cf6a95bfd36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/p-hoffmann/trexsql-ext/git/trees/ce32f068ae2b39cb3baa1850ca829cf6a95bfd36"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/p-hoffmann/trexsql-ext/git/commits/c33d8cf81bc4a9b137ae3553ecc95fe30c5e587b","verification":{"payload":"tree ce32f068ae2b39cb3baa1850ca829cf6a95bfd36\nparent 64b524bc042a6921bd99dc3f339230c2c0f9b2da\nauthor Peter Hoffmann <954078+p-hoffmann@users.noreply.github.com> 1771256864 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1771256864 +0800\n\ncombine dockerfiles (#71)\n\nThis pull request makes several improvements to the Docker build process, extension management, and the build pipeline for the `cql2elm` extension. The most impactful changes include streamlining how extensions are handled in Docker, updating the `.dockerignore` to better reflect new extension sources, and introducing a robust build process for the `cql2elm` extension. Additionally, the web admin interface for extensions is improved for clarity, and dependencies are updated for easier extension management.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpkzwgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1HYQAGxAaET32M5RyAe9PfY7x81h\n/uVQZrdgYQXareP6EBWih1ZbpowhnwNW+0ueFt9L/lpy3oiPuuQdNSRe/FH0LP5G\nTpyQM1VJHHYx5G1FS44B9MMdTK4BBPUegCYx0kdoIrpT/Gub6oi5x81F/o4ubRlh\n37fZnvmvFWNICmnE6CtYWth+lIEmdWIHjb9dofR5VU0KH+Ufm8YUxJd5O+NUV5f6\nKJCMEKchOZf2hw0oh+STyg+ArtRWPecraNcAx+K1TXKSPzeT11Yk2sRV2HvWfvic\nMu08eRQxEMqzNyXLz7+ELOWy9nQVTVTh/gcflRL4JJK9EbzSsp7iSwzG+cEsdG6c\nG86jfcvSqX7Kf/1eC8iCRniF/1vIwPS3cPOY+bVV6nmv5nNNUi9u/d4KRFNIeFSk\noYrf0kYM6zhLCBREO9+IOBVUwr0VI5thUof64dUtEVhPHoC081AnOYUuavPh8A76\n5PUVQhELvHFkMg7Bp9KQ6SXWj9ewS3Tvpw7bTPL6yMa5fIPKvD7GATlA+7WuXt6d\niZtDR1jkiNJD3N7PauTYLBTZruWcSw1jhQFHwsj5qSEk/oQfvjcDihKFusAPP9/M\nu3L7UF0udxRJv3oT