":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/a0a7c79def06994bae12b739a3724ebbcc624d19/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T22:13:48Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T22:13:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(collision): publish ARPA targets under targets.* (#138)\n\n## Summary\n\n- After review, the Signal K Targets API (SignalK/signalk-server#3124)\nis being replaced by a data-model convention: radar and camera targets\nare ordinary `targets.<type>:<id>` contexts, and a fusion plugin links\neach one to its AIS vessel with `sameAs`.\n- ARPA targets are now published as `targets.radar:<radarId>-<n>` deltas\n(position, course, speed). A lost track gets a `null` position. This\nworks on every Signal K server, so chart plotters and history can see\nradar targets too.\n- Because collision-alerts can now see radar targets on any server, the\n\"Leave to the Collision Alerts plugin\" setting no longer falls back to\nCoastal. Its description says to choose it only when that plugin is\ninstalled.\n\n## Tested\n\n- `npm run build:all` passes (205 tests).\n- End to end: signalk-server, the mayara emulator, this branch,\nsignalk-target-fusion and dirkwa/signalk-collision-alerts#11. ARPA\ntargets appeared under `/signalk/v1/api/targets`. An AIS ship placed on\na radar track was linked to it (`sameAs`) and raised a single alarm.\nWhen its AIS went quiet, the alarm kept the vessel id because radar\nstill tracked it.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n## Summary\n- Publishes ARPA targets as Signal K deltas under\n`targets.radar:<radarId>-<n>`, with position and available finite course\nand speed values.\n- When a target is lost or expires, publishes null position, course, and\nspeed values. Clears published targets when the plugin stops.\n- Keeps radar alarms in this plugin unless the user selects\n`collision-alerts-plugin`. That setting disables local radar alarms. The\nconfiguration warns that radar targets raise no alarm if Collision\nAlerts is selected without the required plugin.\n- Updates tests for target mapping, publication, expiration, shutdown,\nand alarm preset selection.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","tree":{"sha":"be49d81d8787496c585134894334825028873ec0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/trees/be49d81d8787496c585134894334825028873ec0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/commits/a0a7c79def06994bae12b739a3724ebbcc624d19","verification":{"payload":"tree be49d81d8787496c585134894334825028873ec0\nparent 62fe55c3d41e8ca8e7a995b7632b35e2ab74f6f1\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1791324828 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791324828 +1200\n\nfeat(collision): publish ARPA targets under targets.* (#138)\n\n## Summary\n\n- After review, the Signal K Targets API (SignalK/signalk-server#3124)\nis being replaced by a data-model convention: radar and camera targets\nare ordinary `targets.<type>:<id>` contexts, and a fusion plugin links\neach one to its AIS vessel with `sameAs`.\n- ARPA targets are now published as `targets.radar:<radarId>-<n>` deltas\n(position, course, speed). A lost track gets a `null` position. This\nworks on every Signal K server, so chart plotters and history can see\nradar targets too.\n- Because collision-alerts can now see radar targets on any server, the\n\"Leave to the Collision Alerts plugin\" setting no longer falls back to\nCoastal. Its description says to choose it only when that plugin is\ninstalled.\n\n## Tested\n\n- `npm run build:all` passes (205 tests).\n- End to end: signalk-server, the mayara emulator, this branch,\nsignalk-target-fusion and dirkwa/signalk-collision-alerts#11. ARPA\ntargets appeared under `/signalk/v1/api/targets`. An AIS ship placed on\na radar track was linked to it (`sameAs`) and raised a single alarm.\nWhen its AIS went quiet, the alarm kept the vessel id because radar\nstill tracked it.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n## Summary\n- Publishes ARPA targets as Signal K deltas under\n`targets.radar:<radarId>-<n>`, with position and available finite course\nand speed values.\n- When a target is lost or expires, publishes null position, course, and\nspeed values. Clears published targets when the plugin stops.\n- Keeps radar alarms in this plugin unless the user selects\n`collision-alerts-plugin`. That setting disables local radar alarms. The\nconfiguration warns that radar targets raise no alarm if Collision\nAlerts is selected without the required plugin.\n- Updates tests for target mapping, publication, expiration, shutdown,\nand alarm preset selection.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsF