":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/62fe55c3d41e8ca8e7a995b7632b35e2ab74f6f1","sha":"62fe55c3d41e8ca8e7a995b7632b35e2ab74f6f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/62fe55c3d41e8ca8e7a995b7632b35e2ab74f6f1"}],"sha":"a0a7c79def06994bae12b739a3724ebbcc624d19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/a0a7c79def06994bae12b739a3724ebbcc624d19"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/62fe55c3d41e8ca8e7a995b7632b35e2ab74f6f1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:08:16Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T18:08:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(config): replace invalid stored settings with their defaults (#137)\n\nValidates the stored configuration at `start()` with `typebox/value`. An\ninvalid setting falls back to its default instead of reaching the plugin\nunchecked, and the plugin says so.\n\n## Why\n\n`start()` spread `SCHEMA_DEFAULTS` under whatever Signal K handed it, so\na hand-edited or outdated value went through as is:\n\n- a negative `discoveryPollInterval` got past the `|| 10` fallback, and\nNode then polled mayara every millisecond;\n- an unknown `collisionAlerts` value looked up a preset that does not\nexist;\n- `SCHEMA_DEFAULTS` repeated every `default:` of `ConfigSchema` by hand,\nso the two could drift apart.\n\nThe config panel always saves valid values. These cases come from hand\nedits and configs saved by older versions.\n\n## What changes\n\n- `parseConfig` in `src/config/schema.ts`:\n  - fills in missing settings from their defaults;\n- reports a stored `null` and replaces it, instead of letting `Convert`\nturn it into `false` or the string `\"null\"`;\n- converts values that parse cleanly (`\"6502\"` for a number, `\"true\"`\nfor a boolean);\n- replaces any other invalid setting with its default on its own, so one\nbad field doesn''t cost the rest;\n- drops keys the schema doesn''t define, and never modifies the stored\nobject.\n- `start()` uses it and reports each replaced setting. The log gets the\nsetting, the reason and the default used, never the stored value:\n`mayaraArgs` can carry a Signal K token, and `app.error` writes to the\nserver log as is. The plugin status gets the setting names after\n\"Connected\", next to the existing update hint.\n- `SCHEMA_DEFAULTS` is derived from `ConfigSchema` with `Value.Default`.\n- Four token tests used `reconnectInterval: 0.01` to run fast. That is\nbelow the schema''s one-second minimum and would now be reset, which\nwould have made three of them pass even with cancellation broken. They\nnow use a valid interval and fake timers (a new `loadPlugin` option).\n- AGENTS.md (module map, the defaults gotcha) and the README describe\nthe behaviour.\n\n## Tested\n\n- `npm run build:all`: lint and build pass, 221 tests pass, including\nthe new `test/config-schema.test.ts` and three integration tests: the\nlog line, the status hint, and a token in a rejected `mayaraArgs`\nstaying out of the log.\n- On purpose, I broke the token loop''s cancellation, and \"stops\nre-requesting once the plugin is stopped\" failed. I also advanced the\nfake clock by less than one interval, and \"re-requests on the reconnect\ncadence\" failed.\n- `npm run test:e2e` against signalk-server 2.32.0 and mayara-server\nwith a Furuno DRS4D-NXT: 19/19.\n- On a real Signal K server with `host: null`, `discoveryPollInterval:\n-5`, `collisionAlerts: \"coastel\"` and `port: \"6502\"` stored:\n- the log showed `Setting host must be string; using the default,\n\"localhost\"`, `Setting discoveryPollInterval must be >= 5; using the\ndefault, 10` and `Setting collisionAlerts must be one of off, harbour,\ncoastal, offshore, collision-alerts-plugin; using the default,\n\"coastal\"`;\n- the port was converted without a log line, and the plugin connected to\nboth radars;\n- the plugin status read `Connected - 2 radar(s) · invalid settings\nreplaced by defaults: host, discoveryPollInterval, collisionAlerts`.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary\n\n`parseConfig` builds a complete `Config` from stored settings. It\nconverts values that parse cleanly, replaces invalid or missing values\nwith schema defaults, and removes unknown keys without modifying the\nstored object.\n\nAt startup, the plugin logs each replaced setting with its value,\nreason, and default. It lists replaced setting names in the Connected\nstatus. `SCHEMA_DEFAULTS` comes from `ConfigSchema`.\n\nThe changes add schema parsing tests and integration tests for\nreplacement logs and status hints. Token-recovery tests use fake timers\nand valid reconnect intervals. Documentation describes the fallback\nbehavior.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe supplied objectives report that `npm run build:all` passes lint,\nbuild, and 219 tests. They also report that `npm run test:e2e` passes 19\ntests against signalk-server 2.32.0 and mayara-server.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","tree":{"sha":"c13f1a8651f8ba2387dbb6b502418be83ac6916d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/trees/c13f1a8651f8ba2387dbb6b502418be83ac6916d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/commits/62fe55c3d41e8ca8e7a995b7632b35e2ab74f6f1","verification":{"payload":"tree c13f1a8651f8ba2387dbb6b502418be83ac6916d\nparent df1668b217a8900ca7efd70464ef600570a143c0\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1791223696 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791223696 +1200\n\nfeat(config): replace invalid stored settings with their defaults (#137)\n\nValidates the stored configuration at `start()` with `typebox/value`. An\ninvalid setting falls back to its default instead of reaching the plugin\nunchecked, and the plugin says so.\n\n## Why\n\n`start()` spread `SCHEMA_DEFAULTS` under whatever Signal K handed it, so\na hand-edited or outdated value went through as is:\n\n- a negative `discoveryPollInterval` got past the `|| 10` fallback, and\nNode then polled mayara every millisecond;\n- an unknown `collisionAlerts` value looked up a preset that does not\nexist;\n- `SCHEMA_DEFAULTS` repeated every `default:` of `ConfigSchema` by hand,\nso the two could drift apart.\n\nThe config panel always saves valid values. These cases come from hand\nedits and configs saved by older versions.\n\n## What changes\n\n- `parseConfig` in `src/config/schema.ts`:\n  - fills in missing settings from their defaults;\n- reports a stored `null` and replaces it, instead of letting `Convert`\nturn it into `false` or the string `\"null\"`;\n- converts values that parse cleanly (`\"6502\"` for a number, `\"true\"`\nfor a boolean);\n- replaces any other invalid setting with its default on its own, so one\nbad field doesn''t cost the rest;\n- drops keys the schema doesn''t define, and never modifies the stored\nobject.\n- `start()` uses it and reports each replaced setting. The log gets the\nsetting, the reason and the default used, never the stored value:\n`mayaraArgs` can carry a Signal K token, and `app.error` writes to the\nserver log as is. The plugin status gets the setting names after\n\"Connected\", next to the existing update hint.\n- `SCHEMA_DEFAULTS` is derived from `ConfigSchema` with `Value.Default`.\n- Four token tests used `reconnectInterval: 0.01` to run fast. That is\nbelow the schema''s one-second minimum and would now be reset, which\nwould have made three of them pass even with cancellation broken. They\nnow use a valid interval and fake timers (a new `loadPlugin` option).\n- AGENTS.md (module map, the defaults gotcha) and the README describe\nthe behaviour.\n\n## Tested\n\n- `npm run build:all`: lint and build pass, 221 tests pass, including\nthe new `test/config-schema.test.ts` and three integration tests: the\nlog line, the status hint, and a token in a rejected `mayaraArgs`\nstaying out of the log.\n- On purpose, I broke the token loop''s cancellation, and \"stops\nre-requesting once the plugin is stopped\" failed. I also advanced the\nfake clock by less than one interval, and \"re-requests on the reconnect\ncadence\" failed.\n- `npm run test:e2e` against signalk-server 2.32.0 and mayara-server\nwith a Furuno DRS4D-NXT: 19/19.\n- On a real Signal K server with `host: null`, `discoveryPollInterval:\n-5`, `collisionAlerts: \"coastel\"` and `port: \"6502\"` stored:\n- the log showed `Setting host must be string; using the default,\n\"localhost\"`, `Setting discoveryPollInterval must be >= 5; using the\ndefault, 10` and `Setting collisionAlerts must be one of off, harbour,\ncoastal, offshore, collision-alerts-plugin; using the default,\n\"coastal\"`;\n- the port was converted without a log line, and the plugin connected to\nboth radars;\n- the plugin status read `Connected - 2 radar(s) · invalid settings\nreplaced by defaults: host, discoveryPollInterval, collisionAlerts`.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary\n\n`parseConfig` builds a complete `Config` from stored settings. It\nconverts values that parse cleanly, replaces invalid or missing values\nwith schema defaults, and removes unknown keys without modifying the\nstored object.\n\nAt startup, the plugin logs each replaced setting with its value,\nreason, and default. It lists replaced setting names in the Connected\nstatus. `SCHEMA_DEFAULTS` comes from `ConfigSchema`.\n\nThe changes add schema parsing tests and integration tests for\nreplacement logs and status hints. Token-recovery tests use fake timers\nand valid reconnect intervals. Documentation describes the fallback\nbehavior.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe supplied objectives report that `npm run build:all` passes lint,\nbuild, and 219 tests. They also report that `npm run test:e2e` passes 19\ntests against signalk-server 2.32.0 and mayara-server.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw+eRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEMkQAJ4RcZlf8uHujXJKFEH1sYWG\nPwXrWsWeRJDo9hM/scgnfo5YMi/aot0GK8EcPe0otmGNLMTZw/dfCgexDBgxhsPF\nzV+McahUQ+JFyZQOFBpJ4ZsvftURMA4sjEYSp9zJ6uED5UOFcbzVaWN6bnUWBRgr\njtJUoQgtNmyzva1EGXwk2qUJ2ZlTCkuOKg8OXLbDNX3xe+SwLjuAfX2IvgfRK7Vd\nf4/kMmjgdLVbvHJAItFBEsEuTlxIuK6gBdVYGPn8F3b1tHnOGMURlZcvr6HQV7NT\nY0W7KjAW9rZo9bH5srMUfHG1YVNUcTrMjNukBgv2IeafI2TDM4FJfugVBNoh4/2C\n9tND64kirEvKlXAI+WZ3EiE8Ux2gr/EmtRQm7aQdtXIOxxfyb+P0TwE66houn2Tb\nV+m8Ml6MfUW51ptW9nT0vgFPpyRl9e7VOh0yi3nTd0zLAco07DNwPWRNjMrvPtk3\nDpLR9ce5kIPWlpvvg8RKH29lr/bnU9EyiuMAjBJTa5wJf5YKd+61CwA39rZMhqCm\nQKNpGYZN4zUVsgwtl+XfVeFvLx+8B7NmCz5GsjGhjG3aj/Np6u1fV29VLMcYGgG4\nT86WB+C9GBRNdklf2xdgXehD87fTnIM0at+QavGAsiSoqel24t556XYSb7L04jmN\n2+IzR97ppeLp3P0n+5Yi\n=wWXk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T18:08:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/62fe55c3d41e8ca8e7a995b7632b35e2ab74f6f1","node_id":"C_kwDOQqtUNdoAKDYyZmU1NWMzZDQxZThjYThlN2E5OTViNzYzMmIzNWUyYWI3NGY2ZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/df1668b217a8900ca7efd70464ef600570a143c0","sha":"df1668b217a8900ca7efd70464ef600570a143c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/df1668b217a8900ca7efd70464ef600570a143c0"}],"sha":"62fe55c3d41e8ca8e7a995b7632b35e2ab74f6f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/62fe55c3d41e8ca8e7a995b7632b35e2ab74f6f1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/df1668b217a8900ca7efd70464ef600570a143c0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:56:34Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:56:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(tooling): convert the remaining JavaScript to TypeScript (#139)\n\nConverts the last JavaScript in the repo to TypeScript, so GitHub''s\nlanguage bar shows TypeScript only. GitHub counted 23,602 bytes of\nJavaScript, and those were exactly five tooling files:\n\n| Before | After |\n| --- | --- |\n| `test/e2e/run-e2e.mjs` | `test/e2e/run-e2e.ts`, typed |\n| `build.js` | `build.ts` |\n| `eslint.config.mjs` | `eslint.config.ts` |\n| `prettier.config.mjs` | `prettier.config.ts` |\n| `webpack.config.js` | deleted: nothing has used it since the move to\nVite |\n\nThe tracked `plugin/*.js` build output doesn''t count, because GitHub\nalready treats it as generated.\n\n## How the tooling runs\n\n- Node runs `build.ts` and the e2e harness directly by stripping their\ntypes. That is on by default from Node 22.18 and in 24, so working on\nthe repo now needs one of those. CI already uses the latest 22 and 24.\nThe published plugin is compiled as before and still runs on the\n`engines` floor (22.15).\n- ESLint loads `eslint.config.ts` through `jiti`, a new dev dependency.\nThe config now uses ESLint''s own `defineConfig` instead of the\ndeprecated `tseslint.config`; the resolved config is identical.\n- Prettier loads `prettier.config.ts` natively, and `satisfies Config`\nchecks it.\n\n## Type checking and linting\n\n- `tsconfig.tools.json` type-checks all of the tooling, including\n`vite.config.ts` and `vitest.config.ts`, which nothing checked before.\n`erasableSyntaxOnly` and `verbatimModuleSyntax` make syntax Node cannot\nstrip fail the type check rather than the run. `npm run typecheck:tools`\nruns as part of `build`.\n- The root tooling is now linted under the same strict rules as `src/`;\nbefore, it was ignored.\n- The e2e harness gets real types: JSON response bodies are narrowed\nbefore use instead of flowing through as `any`. Its behaviour is\nunchanged.\n\nAGENTS.md gets a short \"TypeScript tooling\" note and the renamed\nreferences. The README states the Node version needed for building, and\n`.npmignore` and two comments in `vite.config.ts` use the new file\nnames.\n\n## Tested\n\n- `npm run build:all` on Node 24: lint and build pass, 208 tests pass.\n- On Node 22.23, `npm run build`, `npm run lint` and `npm run\nformat:check` pass, with no experimental warnings. On Node 22.14, `node\nbuild.ts` fails with \"Unknown file extension .ts\", as expected below\n22.18.\n- `npm run test:e2e`, the converted harness, against signalk-server\n2.32.0 and mayara-server with a Furuno DRS4D-NXT: 19/19.\n- ESLint''s resolved config (`--print-config`) is byte-identical before\nand after the `defineConfig` change for a server file, the config panel\nand a test.\n- `npm pack --dry-run` lists the same 76 files as on `main`.","tree":{"sha":"3d834ea126d8a30ac2a49330dff5a18f247f1d2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/trees/3d834ea126d8a30ac2a49330dff5a18f247f1d2e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/commits/df1668b217a8900ca7efd70464ef600570a143c0","verification":{"payload":"tree 3d834ea126d8a30ac2a49330dff5a18f247f1d2e\nparent ca1400fd06722c0ff3ba9099d9fc1bc3ca56dd5e\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1791222994 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791222994 +1200\n\nrefactor(tooling): convert the remaining JavaScript to TypeScript (#139)\n\nConverts the last JavaScript in the repo to TypeScript, so GitHub''s\nlanguage bar shows TypeScript only. GitHub counted 23,602 bytes of\nJavaScript, and those were exactly five tooling files:\n\n| Before | After |\n| --- | --- |\n| `test/e2e/run-e2e.mjs` | `test/e2e/run-e2e.ts`, typed |\n| `build.js` | `build.ts` |\n| `eslint.config.mjs` | `eslint.config.ts` |\n| `prettier.config.mjs` | `prettier.config.ts` |\n| `webpack.config.js` | deleted: nothing has used it since the move to\nVite |\n\nThe tracked `plugin/*.js` build output doesn''t count, because GitHub\nalready treats it as generated.\n\n## How the tooling runs\n\n- Node runs `build.ts` and the e2e harness directly by stripping their\ntypes. That is on by default from Node 22.18 and in 24, so working on\nthe repo now needs one of those. CI already uses the latest 22 and 24.\nThe published plugin is compiled as before and still runs on the\n`engines` floor (22.15).\n- ESLint loads `eslint.config.ts` through `jiti`, a new dev dependency.\nThe config now uses ESLint''s own `defineConfig` instead of the\ndeprecated `tseslint.config`; the resolved config is identical.\n- Prettier loads `prettier.config.ts` natively, and `satisfies Config`\nchecks it.\n\n## Type checking and linting\n\n- `tsconfig.tools.json` type-checks all of the tooling, including\n`vite.config.ts` and `vitest.config.ts`, which nothing checked before.\n`erasableSyntaxOnly` and `verbatimModuleSyntax` make syntax Node cannot\nstrip fail the type check rather than the run. `npm run typecheck:tools`\nruns as part of `build`.\n- The root tooling is now linted under the same strict rules as `src/`;\nbefore, it was ignored.\n- The e2e harness gets real types: JSON response bodies are narrowed\nbefore use instead of flowing through as `any`. Its behaviour is\nunchanged.\n\nAGENTS.md gets a short \"TypeScript tooling\" note and the renamed\nreferences. The README states the Node version needed for building, and\n`.npmignore` and two comments in `vite.config.ts` use the new file\nnames.\n\n## Tested\n\n- `npm run build:all` on Node 24: lint and build pass, 208 tests pass.\n- On Node 22.23, `npm run build`, `npm run lint` and `npm run\nformat:check` pass, with no experimental warnings. On Node 22.14, `node\nbuild.ts` fails with \"Unknown file extension .ts\", as expected below\n22.18.\n- `npm run test:e2e`, the converted harness, against signalk-server\n2.32.0 and mayara-server with a Furuno DRS4D-NXT: 19/19.\n- ESLint''s resolved config (`--print-config`) is byte-identical before\nand after the `defineConfig` change for a server file, the config panel\nand a test.\n- `npm pack --dry-run` lists the same 76 files as on `main`.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw+TSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8ggQAG7TLSrT+WJgg/z78edzrNXw\nbbG0TYK3WgR5C9OvD2cABHdNsfjtCBpEjYzitnW5a5veJsjRscv3k25GrDv0LNMf\nG8xcu4ZBlsszyjFEKachZC1u0XYXz/TKtAdNgIu4+xCh3m+rDZuBw3Rcktd3Af67\nZMupNJ+RVfveS0scOMjutqO/BEpOXgUVdvUjadD2iU+n36/9XuMwUQMhUMDnPujH\n7EZegc0rsaylWR+SA8Oxwl9eTJNpvarDYLRT1FknCkp6+EjiHeioIy2qqhLReJMp\n4ahfbBMNqfS94wbjlrJXI4FrXrC4pPwWQwceCfzxICRpFBfHt8VOvXGc7H3c/o45\nHp2a3QhiAWEPCezTPR9yUUo3XMYfE4ACurDxSwz1EXhIZ0LNLRo6AHEukqGwRghF\ns1V4wuxcpG+39FbNy0FRTUXbZx9ntAdbj0ul7dXqJbkfYR76Vq/jyPGObMkfEIxm\nnI5qd2s6gsP0RSNIjkmV2jYRxS4hIU05yiZZ/dzelzI+m18gd89ZeI1xLngkmJE6\nT/rd2ZF37xGolGi5SmEenCN2V4DQHrlOFj21tnwCPN5lT+n1e9zkFunq7BPdzNXb\njB+2EQZnNirnb/NW13jUTZVDbS3sNo8loVW37JDLSrwOAHbrmubAoBoNx/lKmqwx\nqxTisYVMssF4k1umFWMs\n=7HMR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T17:56:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/df1668b217a8900ca7efd70464ef600570a143c0","node_id":"C_kwDOQqtUNdoAKGRmMTY2OGIyMTdhODkwMGNhN2VmZDcwNDY0ZWY2MDA1NzBhMTQzYzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/ca1400fd06722c0ff3ba9099d9fc1bc3ca56dd5e","sha":"ca1400fd06722c0ff3ba9099d9fc1bc3ca56dd5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/ca1400fd06722c0ff3ba9099d9fc1bc3ca56dd5e"}],"sha":"df1668b217a8900ca7efd70464ef600570a143c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/df1668b217a8900ca7efd70464ef600570a143c0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/ca1400fd06722c0ff3ba9099d9fc1bc3ca56dd5e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:54:04Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T17:54:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(build): stop tracking the generated plugin/ output (#140)\n\nStops tracking the compiled `plugin/` output. Eight files there were\ncommitted from before the `.gitignore` rule, while the rest of the\ncompiled output never was.\n\n## Why\n\n- The tracked copies go stale whenever a change doesn''t rebuild and\ncommit them. On `main`, `plugin/index.js` still imports\n`http-proxy-middleware`, which #133 removed.\n- They can''t serve an install from git either. `index.js` imports\n`delta-forwarder.js`, `gui-proxy.js` and `collision/`, none of which was\never tracked.\n- Nothing reads them:\n- `publish.yml` builds from a clean checkout (`git clean -xfd`, then\n`npm run build`) before `npm publish`, and `prepublishOnly` builds too;\n- npm packs `plugin/` from that build, because `.npmignore`, not\n`.gitignore`, decides what ships.\n- `.gitignore` only covered `plugin/*.js` at the top level, so\n`plugin/config/` and `plugin/collision/` showed up as untracked after\nevery build.\n\n## What changes\n\n- The eight `plugin/` files are removed from git (`git rm --cached`; a\nlocal build keeps its copy).\n- `.gitignore` ignores `plugin/` as a whole.\n- AGENTS.md replaces \"rebuild and commit the corresponding `plugin/`\nartifact\" with \"never commit `plugin/` or `public/`\", and explains why\nthe published package is still right.\n- `.coderabbit.yaml`:\n- drops the `!plugin/**` path filter and the line saying the release PR\ntracks `plugin/`;\n- replaces the `public/**` instruction, which described `public/` as the\nconfig-panel sources and webpack as the bundler, with instructions that\nflag any PR adding files to `plugin/` or `public/`. Without the filter,\nCodeRabbit can now see such a file.\n- `.prettierignore`''s comment no longer calls the output tracked or\nwebpack-built.\n\n#138 edits three of these files (`plugin/index.js`,\n`plugin/config/schema.js` and its map), following the old AGENTS.md\nrule. Whichever of the two merges second gets a modify/delete conflict\non them; resolve it by keeping the files deleted.\n\n## Tested\n\n- `npm run build:all`: lint and build pass, 208 tests pass.\n- `npm pack --dry-run` lists the same 76 files as on `main`, 56 of them\nunder `plugin/`.\n- `npm run test:e2e` against signalk-server 2.32.0 and mayara-server\nwith a Furuno DRS4D-NXT: 19/19. The harness installs the packed plugin,\nso this covers the package built without tracked `plugin/` files.\n- `.coderabbit.yaml` parses, with the new `plugin/**` and `public/**`\ninstructions in place.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n- Removes eight tracked files from `plugin/` and ignores the directory\nand its subdirectories.\n- Updates `AGENTS.md`, `.coderabbit.yaml`, and `.prettierignore` to\nidentify `plugin/` and `public/` as generated build output. CodeRabbit\nnow flags added files in these directories instead of filtering them\nfrom review.\n- The author reports that publishing builds from a clean checkout and\nthat the packed file list is unchanged. The author also reports passing\nbuild, test, end-to-end, and configuration checks.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","tree":{"sha":"049203f42ca108db9a1d0f44f2eb90851a853bca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/trees/049203f42ca108db9a1d0f44f2eb90851a853bca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/commits/ca1400fd06722c0ff3ba9099d9fc1bc3ca56dd5e","verification":{"payload":"tree 049203f42ca108db9a1d0f44f2eb90851a853bca\nparent 45b3edbc14640d866d6322f0c6cdf1999462c926\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1791222844 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791222844 +1200\n\nchore(build): stop tracking the generated plugin/ output (#140)\n\nStops tracking the compiled `plugin/` output. Eight files there were\ncommitted from before the `.gitignore` rule, while the rest of the\ncompiled output never was.\n\n## Why\n\n- The tracked copies go stale whenever a change doesn''t rebuild and\ncommit them. On `main`, `plugin/index.js` still imports\n`http-proxy-middleware`, which #133 removed.\n- They can''t serve an install from git either. `index.js` imports\n`delta-forwarder.js`, `gui-proxy.js` and `collision/`, none of which was\never tracked.\n- Nothing reads them:\n- `publish.yml` builds from a clean checkout (`git clean -xfd`, then\n`npm run build`) before `npm publish`, and `prepublishOnly` builds too;\n- npm packs `plugin/` from that build, because `.npmignore`, not\n`.gitignore`, decides what ships.\n- `.gitignore` only covered `plugin/*.js` at the top level, so\n`plugin/config/` and `plugin/collision/` showed up as untracked after\nevery build.\n\n## What changes\n\n- The eight `plugin/` files are removed from git (`git rm --cached`; a\nlocal build keeps its copy).\n- `.gitignore` ignores `plugin/` as a whole.\n- AGENTS.md replaces \"rebuild and commit the corresponding `plugin/`\nartifact\" with \"never commit `plugin/` or `public/`\", and explains why\nthe published package is still right.\n- `.coderabbit.yaml`:\n- drops the `!plugin/**` path filter and the line saying the release PR\ntracks `plugin/`;\n- replaces the `public/**` instruction, which described `public/` as the\nconfig-panel sources and webpack as the bundler, with instructions that\nflag any PR adding files to `plugin/` or `public/`. Without the filter,\nCodeRabbit can now see such a file.\n- `.prettierignore`''s comment no longer calls the output tracked or\nwebpack-built.\n\n#138 edits three of these files (`plugin/index.js`,\n`plugin/config/schema.js` and its map), following the old AGENTS.md\nrule. Whichever of the two merges second gets a modify/delete conflict\non them; resolve it by keeping the files deleted.\n\n## Tested\n\n- `npm run build:all`: lint and build pass, 208 tests pass.\n- `npm pack --dry-run` lists the same 76 files as on `main`, 56 of them\nunder `plugin/`.\n- `npm run test:e2e` against signalk-server 2.32.0 and mayara-server\nwith a Furuno DRS4D-NXT: 19/19. The harness installs the packed plugin,\nso this covers the package built without tracked `plugin/` files.\n- `.coderabbit.yaml` parses, with the new `plugin/**` and `public/**`\ninstructions in place.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n- Removes eight tracked files from `plugin/` and ignores the directory\nand its subdirectories.\n- Updates `AGENTS.md`, `.coderabbit.yaml`, and `.prettierignore` to\nidentify `plugin/` and `public/` as generated build output. CodeRabbit\nnow flags added files in these directories instead of filtering them\nfrom review.\n- The author reports that publishing builds from a clean checkout and\nthat the packed file list is unchanged. The author also reports passing\nbuild, test, end-to-end, and configuration checks.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw+Q8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPu4QACI+9w/KgBET5nH5TsqoviGB\n8C4dM/vQ/CegjDmaySdKcYw06KaVayNQHbcFxwCHFIlOI8dnvciz3abFXqJCSMyH\nOnAcxmQ4HSl0l5LpFZnH/2KAgM673Q1z8XFz4tLhZSUUtxdf3AHEOX7vgcdavaAm\nDf9ETWSxjjdbFoaX3NU6zQkiA2KSFS6SSFouAW0+W53KRYP+vcCsqwToCTQRTfIQ\nlVxcVbjS3USX2muyLXhAZqhs2+vvq0qr7wr3QlbejPKzAz+MyC5HCKtOePCEz9G6\nr7aZVDUjQDf/JXWXDbfYV4sPW0ItybHLjfM+uQGWAE0Iae4+cmj1nvE5as+p3QpD\nbtgzEknaRmi3mvbOWvdS0GRG4gisE4me5xFrcqqGd0QLJgsvN12EqlaAyXlrRmJX\neQCyxeWDz7LkhV9R4enr6a5Pxkudq9BEMdZW7t+gfi7QNWVFR3jIZ4gor+CabxU2\nSWjxZggBnpe7rDXCVIKYK0ySnEaVud8z4JgbZg0qKHVspo0Ds64sqpwh5jRqOWJq\ny7ysk+q36qa9mY7lTjwgK66uF1zaWR9cs8UDzz6RLOFYVIK2HWF2qm9sUPm+7kJL\nC6jyzTLynDhg8VGr+RYQALd0UzUYHVnGzOAvPMg9mhAt8y7zhImmWMjj4MRC0Fot\nKZcsfx4uN/qx+je4jMBC\n=4frK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T17:54:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/ca1400fd06722c0ff3ba9099d9fc1bc3ca56dd5e","node_id":"C_kwDOQqtUNdoAKGNhMTQwMGZkMDY3MjJjMGZmM2JhOTA5OWQ5ZmMxYmMzY2E1NmRkNWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/45b3edbc14640d866d6322f0c6cdf1999462c926","sha":"45b3edbc14640d866d6322f0c6cdf1999462c926","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/45b3edbc14640d866d6322f0c6cdf1999462c926"}],"sha":"ca1400fd06722c0ff3ba9099d9fc1bc3ca56dd5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/ca1400fd06722c0ff3ba9099d9fc1bc3ca56dd5e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/45b3edbc14640d866d6322f0c6cdf1999462c926/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T04:28:30Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T04:28:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(configpanel): keep directGuiUrl and requestSignalkToken on save (#136)\n\nThe config panel neither shows nor saves `directGuiUrl` and\n`requestSignalkToken`. The Admin UI replaces the stored configuration\nwith whatever the panel''s `save()` passes, so every save drops both\nsettings and `start()` falls back to their defaults (both `true`).\n\nThe visible effect: **Open the radar GUI directly on mayara-server**\ncan''t be turned off from the UI, even though the README tells installs\nthat rely on the Signal K proxy (only the Signal K port open, or a\nTLS-encrypted radar session) to disable it. A hand-edited `false`\nreverts on the next save. `requestSignalkToken` behaves the same way.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Two new toggles:\n- \"Open GUI directly on mayara-server\", in the Connection section next\nto \"Use HTTPS/WSS\";\n- \"Request Signal K token\", in the managed-container block, the only\nmode that requests a token.\n- The panel now types its configuration with `Config` from\n`src/config/schema.ts`. It used to keep its own copy (`PanelConfig`),\nwhich had fallen behind the schema. `save()` now takes a full `Config`,\nso a setting the panel forgets fails `npm run typecheck:panel`. The\nimport is type-only, and the built bundle contains no TypeBox code.\n\n## Tested\n\n- `npm run build:all`: lint and build pass, 208 tests pass.\n- Removing `directGuiUrl` from the `save()` call fails `typecheck:panel`\nwith \"Property ''directGuiUrl'' is missing\".\n- In the Signal K Admin UI (signalk-server 2.32.0), driven by\nPlaywright, with both settings set to `false` in the stored config:\n- on current `main`, one press of Save Configuration removed both keys\nfrom the stored config;\n- on this branch, the toggles showed unchecked and Save kept both\n`false`. Turning \"Open GUI directly\" back on saved `true`, and the token\nsetting stayed `false`.\n- `npm run test:e2e` against mayara-server with a Furuno DRS4D-NXT:\n19/19.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe Connection section with the new toggle switched off, which routes\nthe GUI through Signal K:\n\n<img\nsrc=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dirkwa/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/a592c189596e36d29a7d77d4e0726fe8dba73c82/136/pr-connection.png\"\nalt=\"Connection section with the new Open GUI directly on mayara-server\ntoggle switched off\" width=\"509\">\n\nThe managed-container block with the new token toggle:\n\n<img\nsrc=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dirkwa/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/a592c189596e36d29a7d77d4e0726fe8dba73c82/136/pr-managed.png\"\nalt=\"Managed-container block with the new Request Signal K token toggle\"\nwidth=\"509\">\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary\n\n- Type the configuration panel with the shared `Config` type. The save\ncallback receives the complete configuration.\n- Add `requestSignalkToken` and `directGuiUrl` checkboxes. Both default\nto enabled unless explicitly set to `false`.\n- Include both settings when saving, so the Admin UI preserves them when\nit replaces the stored configuration.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe PR objectives report that `npm run build:all` passes, with 208 tests\npassing. They also report that Playwright checks preserve both settings\nand that `npm run test:e2e` passes 19/19 tests against mayara-server\nwith a Furuno DRS4D-NXT.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","tree":{"sha":"4f3787fffd07fb108988027e8ee1eb9bc95d7b5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/trees/4f3787fffd07fb108988027e8ee1eb9bc95d7b5e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/commits/45b3edbc14640d866d6322f0c6cdf1999462c926","verification":{"payload":"tree 4f3787fffd07fb108988027e8ee1eb9bc95d7b5e\nparent 083c6b43623813bc455f9fe9585b663dd01c73ea\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1791174510 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791174510 +1200\n\nfix(configpanel): keep directGuiUrl and requestSignalkToken on save (#136)\n\nThe config panel neither shows nor saves `directGuiUrl` and\n`requestSignalkToken`. The Admin UI replaces the stored configuration\nwith whatever the panel''s `save()` passes, so every save drops both\nsettings and `start()` falls back to their defaults (both `true`).\n\nThe visible effect: **Open the radar GUI directly on mayara-server**\ncan''t be turned off from the UI, even though the README tells installs\nthat rely on the Signal K proxy (only the Signal K port open, or a\nTLS-encrypted radar session) to disable it. A hand-edited `false`\nreverts on the next save. `requestSignalkToken` behaves the same way.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Two new toggles:\n- \"Open GUI directly on mayara-server\", in the Connection section next\nto \"Use HTTPS/WSS\";\n- \"Request Signal K token\", in the managed-container block, the only\nmode that requests a token.\n- The panel now types its configuration with `Config` from\n`src/config/schema.ts`. It used to keep its own copy (`PanelConfig`),\nwhich had fallen behind the schema. `save()` now takes a full `Config`,\nso a setting the panel forgets fails `npm run typecheck:panel`. The\nimport is type-only, and the built bundle contains no TypeBox code.\n\n## Tested\n\n- `npm run build:all`: lint and build pass, 208 tests pass.\n- Removing `directGuiUrl` from the `save()` call fails `typecheck:panel`\nwith \"Property ''directGuiUrl'' is missing\".\n- In the Signal K Admin UI (signalk-server 2.32.0), driven by\nPlaywright, with both settings set to `false` in the stored config:\n- on current `main`, one press of Save Configuration removed both keys\nfrom the stored config;\n- on this branch, the toggles showed unchecked and Save kept both\n`false`. Turning \"Open GUI directly\" back on saved `true`, and the token\nsetting stayed `false`.\n- `npm run test:e2e` against mayara-server with a Furuno DRS4D-NXT:\n19/19.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThe Connection section with the new toggle switched off, which routes\nthe GUI through Signal K:\n\n<img\nsrc=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dirkwa/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/a592c189596e36d29a7d77d4e0726fe8dba73c82/136/pr-connection.png\"\nalt=\"Connection section with the new Open GUI directly on mayara-server\ntoggle switched off\" width=\"509\">\n\nThe managed-container block with the new token toggle:\n\n<img\nsrc=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dirkwa/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/a592c189596e36d29a7d77d4e0726fe8dba73c82/136/pr-managed.png\"\nalt=\"Managed-container block with the new Request Signal K token toggle\"\nwidth=\"509\">\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary\n\n- Type the configuration panel with the shared `Config` type. The save\ncallback receives the complete configuration.\n- Add `requestSignalkToken` and `directGuiUrl` checkboxes. Both default\nto enabled unless explicitly set to `false`.\n- Include both settings when saving, so the Admin UI preserves them when\nit replaces the stored configuration.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe PR objectives report that `npm run build:all` passes, with 208 tests\npassing. They also report that Playwright checks preserve both settings\nand that `npm run test:e2e` passes 19/19 tests against mayara-server\nwith a Furuno DRS4D-NXT.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwydvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnQAQAHdCfk/m8Gr1Xv9yO0unwCqN\nKKtx/BtmJEiuUjIz/klNoDTPIc/xXSwaYGlWaJw6kOfj96oVoHLMWQq3by8Mb+J+\ncdNzbQ2J2BMelLTXdErLFM6T3hAw75/mE/Ml8s+Van63nlP3B5zUIPQ7m/eYFIbl\n9B3Vy0w3fh3YUxkhXcGbV/QHwNMvCFhgdV39nUR3JF3WHGrggFMljs/JmzeO4A5X\nwI7F6lGRP0C4BxaIHijxPugC/5rnd11HmQh7Ff4XoE3bPnjA4ICh622eLqmRBAWs\nqY7cQRdA8rUk5jVB7IX58kOK9BQhgiLhm6FYzmDArjvYAAvBJbg0E+7815NuKzNY\nBwjE41vk8PYWhShD1qSevKdm43ijcIxTyAaiG2iH+Uxdk3wLUyqyQerTCCgwa/t6\npw9VaD1m61ycsJhSIgci581wQlMO2l+FUZ3PkIDhMC6VilC7VAI68oAjDyZu4//B\nfqjJYIyUcUn6qq058q5Y4m+nD+/4xSZIwxUQtgMM0xMAodhq4wvfMeQJJdutGcb1\nroyM2ILPD9KI7Zc8M7RhwitoP/IjJBvTdH7add4RWE3X/AVbf+2bpyxv2fNhxmoR\nExRxBEHJpNAF28iOC5H9VzOXAGG0mDmRFOUy59faKzqXKs3IEfyEH34BSo+NEWoW\nV5SBaX1xRdRZDIXD3iUE\n=MXHJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T04:28:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/45b3edbc14640d866d6322f0c6cdf1999462c926","node_id":"C_kwDOQqtUNdoAKDQ1YjNlZGJjMTQ2NDBkODY2ZDYzMjJmMGM2Y2RmMTk5OTQ2MmM5MjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/083c6b43623813bc455f9fe9585b663dd01c73ea","sha":"083c6b43623813bc455f9fe9585b663dd01c73ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/083c6b43623813bc455f9fe9585b663dd01c73ea"}],"sha":"45b3edbc14640d866d6322f0c6cdf1999462c926","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/45b3edbc14640d866d6322f0c6cdf1999462c926"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/083c6b43623813bc455f9fe9585b663dd01c73ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T03:08:39Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T03:08:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(gui-proxy): drop the radar-list stream URL rewrite (#135)\n\nRemoves the GUI proxy''s rewrite of `streamUrl` / `spokeDataUrl` in the\nradar list. Since the v3.4.0 Radar API (#90) no radar list contains\nthose fields, so the rewrite never changes anything. This is the\nfollow-up announced in #133.\n\n## Why it is dead\n\n- The proxy sends every `/signalk/…` request, including the radar list,\nto Signal K rather than to mayara. So only Signal K''s response matters.\n- The plugin''s own `getRadarInfo` deliberately leaves both fields out\n(`src/radar-provider.ts`, since #90).\n- No supported signalk-server release has them: no file under `src/` or\n`packages/` mentions `streamUrl` or `spokeDataUrl` in v2.31.0, v2.31.1,\nv2.32.0 or v2.33.0. `RadarInfo` in `@signalk/server-api` documents that\nboth streams are reached by convention from the host that served the\nresponse.\n- The GUI builds both WebSocket URLs from its own location (`wsBase()`\nin mayara''s `api.js`), and `control.js` / `viewer.js` use that whenever\nthey are given no stream URL.\n\n## What changes\n\n- `src/index.ts` drops `rewriteStreamUrl`, `rewriteRadarList` and the\n`jsonRewriter` option.\n- `src/gui-proxy.ts` drops the buffered path: the rewriter lookup,\nremoving `accept-encoding` on rewritten requests, and `sendRewritten`.\nEvery response, the radar list and control PUT replies included, now\nstreams straight through.\n- `test/gui-proxy.test.ts` drops the five rewriter tests.\n- AGENTS.md: the `gui-proxy.ts` entry in the module map no longer\nmentions the rewrite.\n\n`docs/api-divergence.md` still refers to `rewriteStreamUrl` in its\ncomparison table. I left that alone: the document is marked as a\nhistorical record of the pre-3.4.0 state, and its outcome section\nalready says neither stream URL is published.\n\n## Tested\n\n- `npm run build:all`: lint and build pass, 208 tests pass.\n- `npm run test:e2e` against signalk-server 2.32.0 and mayara-server\nwith a Furuno DRS4D-NXT (two antennas): 19/19, including \"RadarInfo is\nthe lean v3.4.0 shape\".\n- By hand through `/plugins/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/gui/` on plain\nHTTP:\n- the radar list loaded (`{ version: \"3.4.0\", radars }`, no stream\nURLs);\n  - a gain PUT, set to its current value, answered 200 in 26 ms;\n  - the control stream received 81 messages in 2 s;\n  - the spoke stream delivered binary frames (about 1.1 MB in 3 s).","tree":{"sha":"9b650fba13cd2787ecd894657285335cbf450a9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/trees/9b650fba13cd2787ecd894657285335cbf450a9f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/commits/083c6b43623813bc455f9fe9585b663dd01c73ea","verification":{"payload":"tree 9b650fba13cd2787ecd894657285335cbf450a9f\nparent 1781f0d5fe82b985b1af7e19643508f052bf7a13\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1791169719 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791169719 +1200\n\nrefactor(gui-proxy): drop the radar-list stream URL rewrite (#135)\n\nRemoves the GUI proxy''s rewrite of `streamUrl` / `spokeDataUrl` in the\nradar list. Since the v3.4.0 Radar API (#90) no radar list contains\nthose fields, so the rewrite never changes anything. This is the\nfollow-up announced in #133.\n\n## Why it is dead\n\n- The proxy sends every `/signalk/…` request, including the radar list,\nto Signal K rather than to mayara. So only Signal K''s response matters.\n- The plugin''s own `getRadarInfo` deliberately leaves both fields out\n(`src/radar-provider.ts`, since #90).\n- No supported signalk-server release has them: no file under `src/` or\n`packages/` mentions `streamUrl` or `spokeDataUrl` in v2.31.0, v2.31.1,\nv2.32.0 or v2.33.0. `RadarInfo` in `@signalk/server-api` documents that\nboth streams are reached by convention from the host that served the\nresponse.\n- The GUI builds both WebSocket URLs from its own location (`wsBase()`\nin mayara''s `api.js`), and `control.js` / `viewer.js` use that whenever\nthey are given no stream URL.\n\n## What changes\n\n- `src/index.ts` drops `rewriteStreamUrl`, `rewriteRadarList` and the\n`jsonRewriter` option.\n- `src/gui-proxy.ts` drops the buffered path: the rewriter lookup,\nremoving `accept-encoding` on rewritten requests, and `sendRewritten`.\nEvery response, the radar list and control PUT replies included, now\nstreams straight through.\n- `test/gui-proxy.test.ts` drops the five rewriter tests.\n- AGENTS.md: the `gui-proxy.ts` entry in the module map no longer\nmentions the rewrite.\n\n`docs/api-divergence.md` still refers to `rewriteStreamUrl` in its\ncomparison table. I left that alone: the document is marked as a\nhistorical record of the pre-3.4.0 state, and its outcome section\nalready says neither stream URL is published.\n\n## Tested\n\n- `npm run build:all`: lint and build pass, 208 tests pass.\n- `npm run test:e2e` against signalk-server 2.32.0 and mayara-server\nwith a Furuno DRS4D-NXT (two antennas): 19/19, including \"RadarInfo is\nthe lean v3.4.0 shape\".\n- By hand through `/plugins/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/gui/` on plain\nHTTP:\n- the radar list loaded (`{ version: \"3.4.0\", radars }`, no stream\nURLs);\n  - a gain PUT, set to its current value, answered 200 in 26 ms;\n  - the control stream received 81 messages in 2 s;\n  - the spoke stream delivered binary frames (about 1.1 MB in 3 s).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwxS3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAozMQAHMcbf2G+wzBsakynaL5rWV9\n1fM83y8jpmhUBb4B3r+1UrESKF1E7eTRYfPPqb5S3iolirMOkfuu89HgL2d4UPg8\ndB6UAaFNdlGK2cgGet+sE/3nFtv2zxhcOSQwtyiGupphOKcsCumVjPwYQEQkbgrR\nn633DabvXeZHq6FJ718tJ869UMXQMY/omC1bZWQfXyuQmiMNGb7yPcc+xFeQiezv\nkU2a05hXPMfb6CfKHes/jqJFFSVk2JfIM4bXgrKuyXStIWkcSkCzYjeCbItQ1uw1\nPIkBBjirCX9IVLdvcDD42Td77ljw9CTc9ihdiHkMu/TkLrf3P2d8eKw98yE+XD/O\ndP7BgISOmbgwn6GuxOwNxauFcg4jeBPdtpT9cfuyFrFaKV++Tswh2rgLV7VzMQon\nlgHHLatV4+yK4vkFAkY54145NpQtO4tjy4gXwsZWvyPpd5eolQOw6NjNJU5MqYyR\nYANbSr5C5TSfEGic5+0ej0PdZDMVkQ7bkOCmNx+FLj+OitFDDt7/2o86Q2KObx9c\nTOjxqRIHL4Y+nXH4om715hX5EQMVbZ1gN4wFHYG2LjTAB3h0EnZEG+hk3k0B6BuP\n2xtMpaTmfxpKigoRA+U+3wmkegC02WFTEjiZNx7qTRYXpWqzEQT5pzqQSCC+eTUb\np90rIA1DHAMlK56J+TRS\n=+UkK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T03:08:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/083c6b43623813bc455f9fe9585b663dd01c73ea","node_id":"C_kwDOQqtUNdoAKDA4M2M2YjQzNjIzODEzYmM0NTVmOWZlOTU4NWI2NjNkZDAxYzczZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/1781f0d5fe82b985b1af7e19643508f052bf7a13","sha":"1781f0d5fe82b985b1af7e19643508f052bf7a13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/1781f0d5fe82b985b1af7e19643508f052bf7a13"}],"sha":"083c6b43623813bc455f9fe9585b663dd01c73ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/083c6b43623813bc455f9fe9585b663dd01c73ea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/1781f0d5fe82b985b1af7e19643508f052bf7a13/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T02:57:14Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T02:57:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(gui-proxy): replace http-proxy-middleware with httpxy (#133)\n\nReplaces `http-proxy-middleware` with `httpxy`, the proxy engine it\nalready wraps, so the installed plugin no longer depends on `braces`.\n\n## Why\n\nThe Signal K plugin registry scores 1.5.5 at 90 instead of 100. The\n`audit-high` deduction is four findings, all one advisory: `braces`\nCVE-2026-93687 (GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm), reached through\n`http-proxy-middleware` → `micromatch` → `braces`. 1.6.0 has the same\nchain.\n\n- No `braces` release fixes it: every version up to 3.0.3, the latest,\nis affected. The fix PRs (micromatch/braces#72, #75) are unmerged, and\nthe maintainers haven''t responded on them or on the CVE issues.\n- `http-proxy-middleware` has declined to drop `micromatch`\n(chimurai/http-proxy-middleware#1284, #1294).\n- The plugin never runs the affected code: `micromatch` only matches a\nglob `pathFilter`, and the GUI proxy sets none. npm `overrides` don''t\napply when the plugin is installed as a dependency, so dropping the\ndependency is the only fix the registry sees.\n\n## What changes\n\n- `src/gui-proxy.ts` (new) provides `createGuiProxy`, built directly on\n`httpxy`. It takes over what the plugin used from the middleware:\n- re-sending a request body that Signal K''s `express.json()` has already\nread (control PUTs hang without it);\n  - rewriting the stream URLs in the radar list;\n- answering an unreachable upstream with 504, and other proxy failures\nwith 502 (the middleware answered those with 500).\n  \nIt also strips the brackets from an IPv6 target, which `httpxy` would\notherwise look up in DNS.\n- `src/index.ts` keeps the same routing (the Signal K loopback for\n`/signalk/…`, mayara for everything else) and the same radar-list\nrewrite, now passed to `createGuiProxy`.\n- Responses that aren''t rewritten now stream through instead of being\nbuffered whole.\n- `test/gui-proxy.test.ts` runs the proxy between real HTTP and\nWebSocket servers. It replaces the test that searched `index.ts` for\n`fixRequestBody`.\n- AGENTS.md: the module map lists `gui-proxy.ts`, the GUI proxy section\ndrops the `ws: false` trap (it belonged to the middleware), and the\nDependencies section explains why `http-proxy-middleware` is gone. The\nREADME no longer gives the middleware as the reason for the Node floor.\n\nThe radar-list rewrite has had nothing to rewrite since the v3.4.0 Radar\nAPI (#90). I''ll remove it in a separate PR once this one merges.\n\n## Tested\n\n- `npm run build:all`: lint and build pass, 213 tests pass.\n- I broke each of these on purpose and the matching test failed: the\nbody re-send, the IPv6 bracket strip, dropping `accept-encoding` on\nrewritten requests, and the 504 status.\n- `npm run test:e2e` against signalk-server 2.32.0 and mayara-server\nwith a Furuno DRS4D-NXT (two antennas): 19/19.\n- By hand through `/plugins/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/gui/`, once on\nplain HTTP and once with SSL enabled (self-signed loopback):\n  - a gain PUT, set to its current value, answered 200 in about 70 ms;\n  - the control stream and the heading stream connected;\n  - the spoke stream delivered binary frames (about 1 MB in 3 s);\n  - the radar list, `viewer.html` and the GUI scripts loaded.\n- A fresh `--omit=dev` install of the packed tarball: `npm audit`\nreports 0 vulnerabilities. The runtime tree is `httpxy`,\n`signalk-container-helper`, `typebox` and `ws`.\n\nOnce this is released, I''ll ask the registry for a rescore.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary\n\n- Replace `http-proxy-middleware` with `httpxy` to remove the `braces`\ndependency chain associated with CVE-2026-93687.\n- Add `createGuiProxy` for HTTP and WebSocket forwarding. It resolves\nthe upstream target per request, strips the GUI mount prefix, and\nforwards request bodies already parsed by Express.\n- Preserve radar-list stream URL rewriting. Stream other responses\nwithout buffering unless JSON rewriting applies.\n- Return 504 for selected upstream connection failures and 502 for other\nproxy failures. Strip brackets from IPv6 targets.\n- Update proxy documentation and add HTTP and WebSocket tests for\nforwarding, rewriting, error handling, and body parsing.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe provided report states that `npm run build:all` passes lint, build\nchecks, and 213 tests. It also reports that `npm run test:e2e` passes 19\ntests and that a fresh production install has 0 reported npm audit\nvulnerabilities.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","tree":{"sha":"69630db0951bb2bf251401cb6fa1865884be2262","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/trees/69630db0951bb2bf251401cb6fa1865884be2262"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/commits/1781f0d5fe82b985b1af7e19643508f052bf7a13","verification":{"payload":"tree 69630db0951bb2bf251401cb6fa1865884be2262\nparent 32bd84449cd7040fe1f12314abaeb781955c3d62\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1791169034 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791169034 +1200\n\nfix(gui-proxy): replace http-proxy-middleware with httpxy (#133)\n\nReplaces `http-proxy-middleware` with `httpxy`, the proxy engine it\nalready wraps, so the installed plugin no longer depends on `braces`.\n\n## Why\n\nThe Signal K plugin registry scores 1.5.5 at 90 instead of 100. The\n`audit-high` deduction is four findings, all one advisory: `braces`\nCVE-2026-93687 (GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm), reached through\n`http-proxy-middleware` → `micromatch` → `braces`. 1.6.0 has the same\nchain.\n\n- No `braces` release fixes it: every version up to 3.0.3, the latest,\nis affected. The fix PRs (micromatch/braces#72, #75) are unmerged, and\nthe maintainers haven''t responded on them or on the CVE issues.\n- `http-proxy-middleware` has declined to drop `micromatch`\n(chimurai/http-proxy-middleware#1284, #1294).\n- The plugin never runs the affected code: `micromatch` only matches a\nglob `pathFilter`, and the GUI proxy sets none. npm `overrides` don''t\napply when the plugin is installed as a dependency, so dropping the\ndependency is the only fix the registry sees.\n\n## What changes\n\n- `src/gui-proxy.ts` (new) provides `createGuiProxy`, built directly on\n`httpxy`. It takes over what the plugin used from the middleware:\n- re-sending a request body that Signal K''s `express.json()` has already\nread (control PUTs hang without it);\n  - rewriting the stream URLs in the radar list;\n- answering an unreachable upstream with 504, and other proxy failures\nwith 502 (the middleware answered those with 500).\n  \nIt also strips the brackets from an IPv6 target, which `httpxy` would\notherwise look up in DNS.\n- `src/index.ts` keeps the same routing (the Signal K loopback for\n`/signalk/…`, mayara for everything else) and the same radar-list\nrewrite, now passed to `createGuiProxy`.\n- Responses that aren''t rewritten now stream through instead of being\nbuffered whole.\n- `test/gui-proxy.test.ts` runs the proxy between real HTTP and\nWebSocket servers. It replaces the test that searched `index.ts` for\n`fixRequestBody`.\n- AGENTS.md: the module map lists `gui-proxy.ts`, the GUI proxy section\ndrops the `ws: false` trap (it belonged to the middleware), and the\nDependencies section explains why `http-proxy-middleware` is gone. The\nREADME no longer gives the middleware as the reason for the Node floor.\n\nThe radar-list rewrite has had nothing to rewrite since the v3.4.0 Radar\nAPI (#90). I''ll remove it in a separate PR once this one merges.\n\n## Tested\n\n- `npm run build:all`: lint and build pass, 213 tests pass.\n- I broke each of these on purpose and the matching test failed: the\nbody re-send, the IPv6 bracket strip, dropping `accept-encoding` on\nrewritten requests, and the 504 status.\n- `npm run test:e2e` against signalk-server 2.32.0 and mayara-server\nwith a Furuno DRS4D-NXT (two antennas): 19/19.\n- By hand through `/plugins/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/gui/`, once on\nplain HTTP and once with SSL enabled (self-signed loopback):\n  - a gain PUT, set to its current value, answered 200 in about 70 ms;\n  - the control stream and the heading stream connected;\n  - the spoke stream delivered binary frames (about 1 MB in 3 s);\n  - the radar list, `viewer.html` and the GUI scripts loaded.\n- A fresh `--omit=dev` install of the packed tarball: `npm audit`\nreports 0 vulnerabilities. The runtime tree is `httpxy`,\n`signalk-container-helper`, `typebox` and `ws`.\n\nOnce this is released, I''ll ask the registry for a rescore.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\n## Summary\n\n- Replace `http-proxy-middleware` with `httpxy` to remove the `braces`\ndependency chain associated with CVE-2026-93687.\n- Add `createGuiProxy` for HTTP and WebSocket forwarding. It resolves\nthe upstream target per request, strips the GUI mount prefix, and\nforwards request bodies already parsed by Express.\n- Preserve radar-list stream URL rewriting. Stream other responses\nwithout buffering unless JSON rewriting applies.\n- Return 504 for selected upstream connection failures and 502 for other\nproxy failures. Strip brackets from IPv6 targets.\n- Update proxy documentation and add HTTP and WebSocket tests for\nforwarding, rewriting, error handling, and body parsing.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe provided report states that `npm run build:all` passes lint, build\nchecks, and 213 tests. It also reports that 