-10-04T18:12:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/32bd84449cd7040fe1f12314abaeb781955c3d62","node_id":"C_kwDOQqtUNdoAKDMyYmQ4NDQ0OWNkNzA0MGZlMWYxMjMxNGFiYWViNzgxOTU1YzNkNjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/b069e5deb2dbe00b19133ae422af8e463e646678","sha":"b069e5deb2dbe00b19133ae422af8e463e646678","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/b069e5deb2dbe00b19133ae422af8e463e646678"}],"sha":"32bd84449cd7040fe1f12314abaeb781955c3d62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/32bd84449cd7040fe1f12314abaeb781955c3d62"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/b069e5deb2dbe00b19133ae422af8e463e646678/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T23:37:26Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T23:37:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(collision): report radar targets to the Signal K Targets API (#131)\n\n## Summary\n\n- A boat seen on both AIS and radar currently raises two collision\nalarms: one from signalk-collision-alerts, one from this plugin. The\nproposed Signal K Targets API (dirkwa/signalk-server#34) merges AIS\nvessels and sensor contacts into one target per boat.\n- On servers that have that API, the plugin now reports each ARPA target\nthere as a `radar` contact (id `<radarId>-<n>`, position, course, speed,\nand a `ref` to `radars.<id>.targets.<n>`). The id uses `-` because the\nserver names a target without AIS `radar:<contact id>`, and with `:`\nthat would equal this plugin''s own alarm key, so both plugins would\nwrite and clear the same notification.\n- Radar alarms stay with this plugin unless the user picks the new radar\nalarm setting *Leave to the Collision Alerts plugin*. Handing them over\nis never automatic, because the collision alerts plugin may not be\ninstalled, and a missing alarm is worse than a duplicate one. On servers\nwithout the API, that choice falls back to the coastal preset.\n- Servers without the API (every released one today) keep today''s radar\nalarms unchanged. The API is feature-detected, so no server version bump\nis needed.\n- Targets are withdrawn when mayara reports them lost, after 30 s of\nsilence on the local clock (a standalone mayara''s clock may differ), and\nwhen the plugin stops.\n\n## Tested\n\n- Unit tests cover the contact mapping, withdrawal when a target is\nlost, expires or the plugin stops, feature detection, and which preset\napplies to radar alarms. `npm run build:all` passes (197 tests).\n- Not yet run against a server carrying the Targets API with a live\nmayara.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\nAdds reporting of valid ARPA targets through Signal K’s Targets API.\nEach contact uses a `<radarId>-<targetId>` ID, includes position and\navailable course and speed, and references the source radar target path.\nThe reporter removes contacts when targets are lost or invalid, expires\nstale contacts, and withdraws all contacts when it stops.\n\nAdds the “Leave to the Collision Alerts plugin” alarm preset. When the\nTargets API is available, the plugin disables its radar collision\nmonitor for this preset. Otherwise, it falls back to the coastal preset.\nThe monitor continues to run by default.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","tree":{"sha":"2211126a79f0a61c77dd0b7d19694044b96251fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/trees/2211126a79f0a61c77dd0b7d19694044b96251fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/commits/b069e5deb2dbe00b19133ae422af8e463e646678","verification":{"payload":"tree 2211126a79f0a61c77dd0b7d19694044b96251fb\nparent a580c1bf1f21cd7d06286c16eb38e27b1d2fa189\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1791070646 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791070646 +1200\n\nfeat(collision): report radar targets to the Signal K Targets API (#131)\n\n## Summary\n\n- A boat seen on both AIS and radar currently raises two collision\nalarms: one from signalk-collision-alerts, one from this plugin. The\nproposed Signal K Targets API (dirkwa/signalk-server#34) merges AIS\nvessels and sensor contacts into one target per boat.\n- On servers that have that API, the plugin now reports each ARPA target\nthere as a `radar` contact (id `<radarId>-<n>`, position, course, speed,\nand a `ref` to `radars.<id>.targets.<n>`). The id uses `-` because the\nserver names a target without AIS `radar:<contact id>`, and with `:`\nthat would equal this plugin''s own alarm key, so both plugins would\nwrite and clear the same notification.\n- Radar alarms stay with this plugin unless the user picks the new radar\nalarm setting *Leave to the Collision Alerts plugin*. Handing them over\nis never automatic, because the collision alerts plugin may not be\ninstalled, and a missing alarm is worse than a duplicate one. On servers\nwithout the API, that choice falls back to the coastal preset.\n- Servers without the API (every released one today) keep today''s radar\nalarms unchanged. The API is feature-detected, so no server version bump\nis needed.\n- Targets are withdrawn when mayara reports them lost, after 30 s of\nsilence on the local clock (a standalone mayara''s clock may differ), and\nwhen the plugin stops.\n\n## Tested\n\n- Unit tests cover the contact mapping, withdrawal when a target is\nlost, expires or the plugin stops, feature detection, and which preset\napplies to radar alarms. `npm run build:all` passes (197 tests).\n- Not yet run against a server carrying the Targets API with a live\nmayara.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai\n-->\n\nAdds reporting of valid ARPA targets through Signal K’s Targets API.\nEach contact uses a `<radarId>-<targetId>` ID, includes position and\navailable course and speed, and references the source radar target path.\nThe reporter removes contacts when targets are lost or invalid, expires\nstale contacts, and withdraws all contacts when it stops.\n\nAdds the “Leave to the Collision Alerts plugin” alarm preset. When the\nTargets API is available, the plugin disables its radar collision\nmonitor for this preset. Otherwise, it falls back to the coastal preset.\nThe monitor continues to run by default.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwZG2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2GsQAEAMSS4iXrTh4esxd9Jcu9iy\nNDPDAZONhGh4BG1PuFS032AAFYbgVofI9XtOMDGfHuuX7RYc0W1Zn7GRPuUWms0E\nNwjJH9zjVjhvFQBMV2diwtONAxnK1lx2s7SE7snGUBrzSdAz//wWE9Vbqtjk80Pa\nYkAqAHz2kWAjmPLloQ5t20TSwML6f9gPmfKxmKGwd5x1uh8uy9OBEEALbSIPWAZJ\nNQWldE0lHWfUXD/EEeSgvAqIR4+Vu96cGyP1sofVfmTqllB0sc+bwRD2cdTsToXn\nz8FmtVqK15RI3tPF6vBVerQUKcO3NjdZ8JgzJ9603kwYY9hMk/aRvvBnCoGkWI1E\nax2YdPnpHeQ267jEwzah/arsR/OiPjCwle/nFeu1+aMJITqNNFU+nNTlMFtXrKa0\nPxghfmQMqzibigI4aWFUpWNSCHR2FXySedXJt/tRfxCByjvQoQg2YRkBCK2SkWZX\nSu2myPoiSAFJ7o6cdP2KvcIrfj2qda4v/zdZ/owzIs09KidGndqlgwJj9d2eEtXv\nXvmpAopaokgkFmqY8fZoD/2YbkT3x4Y6/2wepku6w8ZDXukkH+iQzQs8fspJX/XM\n6Fd03VfCPt4HX1bpW3AiG7wKzv06E+albT0D0kkXHeSGNIIQxx0hkVJs1isqSudJ\nR94TOL0XwAszMrEBIwBv\n=T4tA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T23:37:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/b069e5deb2dbe00b19133ae422af8e463e646678","node_id":"C_kwDOQqtUNdoAKGIwNjllNWRlYjJkYmUwMGIxOTEzM2FlNDIyYWY4ZTQ2M2U2NDY2Nzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/a580c1bf1f21cd7d06286c16eb38e27b1d2fa189","sha":"a580c1bf1f21cd7d06286c16eb38e27b1d2fa189","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/a580c1bf1f21cd7d06286c16eb38e27b1d2fa189"}],"sha":"b069e5deb2dbe00b19133ae422af8e463e646678","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/b069e5deb2dbe00b19133ae422af8e463e646678"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/a580c1bf1f21cd7d06286c16eb38e27b1d2fa189/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:56:49Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:56:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(release): automate releases with release-please (#129)\n\n* ci(release): automate releases with release-please\n\nMerging release-please''s standing `chore(release): X.Y.Z` PR now tags\nthe release, creates the GitHub Release and dispatches publish.yml on\nthe tag, replacing the hand-cut bump PR and tag push.\n\nA gate job runs release-please only for pushes that carry a user-facing\nchange: GitHub-generated notes are never empty, so release-please would\notherwise propose a release after every docs or ci merge. The notes\ncome from GitHub (changelog-type github), so each line names the PR''s\nauthor and links it. label-by-title.yml labels PRs from their\nconventional-commit title for release.yml''s categories, and dependabot\ntitles now separate runtime (build(deps)), dev (build(deps-dev)) and\nActions (ci(deps)) bumps.\n\npublish.yml accepts the dispatch, still creates the Release for a\nhand-pushed pre-release tag, and refuses a tag that does not name\npackage.json''s version.\n\n* ci(release): match release-please''s footer and revert parsing\n\nrelease-please reads a Release-As footer in any case, so the gate\nmust too, or a lowercase footer is silently dropped. GitHub''s own\n\"Revert ...\" PR titles release through the gate but were filed under\nOther; label them as fixes. Dependabot titles are now build(deps),\nbuild(deps-dev) and ci(deps), so CodeRabbit''s title skip list follows.","tree":{"sha":"5fb60d0228f1aa5575f09109322765d5dd4150b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/trees/5fb60d0228f1aa5575f09109322765d5dd4150b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/commits/a580c1bf1f21cd7d06286c16eb38e27b1d2fa189","verification":{"payload":"tree 5fb60d0228f1aa5575f09109322765d5dd4150b6\nparent 7fa48a99a2c89dbc5654396e2b37892e9d34eb0d\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1791068209 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791068209 +1200\n\nci(release): automate releases with release-please (#129)\n\n* ci(release): automate releases with release-please\n\nMerging release-please''s standing `chore(release): X.Y.Z` PR now tags\nthe release, creates the GitHub Release and dispatches publish.yml on\nthe tag, replacing the hand-cut bump PR and tag push.\n\nA gate job runs release-please only for pushes that carry a user-facing\nchange: GitHub-generated notes are never empty, so release-please would\notherwise propose a release after every docs or ci merge. The notes\ncome from GitHub (changelog-type github), so each line names the PR''s\nauthor and links it. label-by-title.yml labels PRs from their\nconventional-commit title for release.yml''s categories, and dependabot\ntitles now separate runtime (build(deps)), dev (build(deps-dev)) and\nActions (ci(deps)) bumps.\n\npublish.yml accepts the dispatch, still creates the Release for a\nhand-pushed pre-release tag, and refuses a tag that does not name\npackage.json''s version.\n\n* ci(release): match release-please''s footer and revert parsing\n\nrelease-please reads a Release-As footer in any case, so the gate\nmust too, or a lowercase footer is silently dropped. GitHub''s own\n\"Revert ...\" PR titles release through the gate but were filed under\nOther; label them as fixes. Dependabot titles are now build(deps),\nbuild(deps-dev) and ci(deps), so CodeRabbit''s title skip list follows.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwYgxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJDoQAGYrMWagbMDfJivT6zM30eZj\nFjJrhPt