121e5fd5b5cf","node_id":"C_kwDOQqtUNdoAKGZiN2ZkODExMWZlYWRhNGY2MTE3NjRmNTAyMzExMjFlNWZkNWI1Y2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/3fb5a0334945f099737438fb06a3ab762f793254","sha":"3fb5a0334945f099737438fb06a3ab762f793254","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/3fb5a0334945f099737438fb06a3ab762f793254"}],"sha":"fb7fd8111feada4f611764f50231121e5fd5b5cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/fb7fd8111feada4f611764f50231121e5fd5b5cf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/3fb5a0334945f099737438fb06a3ab762f793254/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:17:52Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:17:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(controls): exempt radar controls from stale-data enforcement (#124)\n\nA control is a setting, not a measurement: mayara emits one when it\nchanges and then stays quiet. Under signalk-server''s stale-data\nenforcement — 60 s by default — every control on an idle radar was\nblanked to null a minute after the last change, so range, gain and\nautoStandby disappeared from the Data Browser and from any client\nreading them off the stream while the radar was working normally.\n\nDeclare `timeout: 0` for each control path via setDefaultMetadata, the\nsupported way for a plugin to state stale-data behaviour for the paths it\npublishes (SignalK/signalk-server#3025); 0 disables enforcement. The call\ngoes in the existing registerControlPutHandlers loop, which already knows\nevery radar''s exact control paths, rather than on each forwarded delta —\nthe server does not consult delta metadata when resolving a timeout, so\nthat would add traffic and change nothing.\n\nBest-effort: a server without the method throws TypeError, which is\ncaught, leaving the path on the 60 s default — the pre-existing behaviour\n— and never blocking registration of the PUT handler that follows. A\ntimeout the user has set in the Data Browser still wins, which is\nintended; the plugin states a default, not an override.","tree":{"sha":"3822fc2b81d82ed37ae2f4964ff2c84008da21a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/trees/3822fc2b81d82ed37ae2f4964ff2c84008da21a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/commits/3fb5a0334945f099737438fb06a3ab762f793254","verification":{"payload":"tree 3822fc2b81d82ed37ae2f4964ff2c84008da21a2\nparent 9eac9bb5d0db8adf8dc1f82e7aee88753af90f19\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1789345072 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789345072 +0900\n\nfix(controls): exempt radar controls from stale-data enforcement (#124)\n\nA control is a setting, not a measurement: mayara emits one when it\nchanges and then stays quiet. Under signalk-server''s stale-data\nenforcement — 60 s by default — every control on an idle radar was\nblanked to null a minute after the last change, so range, gain and\nautoStandby disappeared from the Data Browser and from any client\nreading them off the stream while the radar was working normally.\n\nDeclare `timeout: 0` for each control path via setDefaultMetadata, the\nsupported way for a plugin to state stale-data behaviour for the paths it\npublishes (SignalK/signalk-server#3025); 0 disables enforcement. The call\ngoes in the existing registerControlPutHandlers loop, which already knows\nevery radar''s exact control paths, rather than on each forwarded delta —\nthe server does not consult delta metadata when resolving a timeout, so\nthat would add traffic and change nothing.\n\nBest-effort: a server without the method throws TypeError, which is\ncaught, leaving the path on the 60 s default — the pre-existing behaviour\n— and never blocking registration of the PUT handler that follows. A\ntimeout the user has set in the Data Browser still wins, which is\nintended; the plugin states a default, not an override.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpz0wCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3jgQAKepHtrH9VTOKImD39dL3r4Q\nPyJfKOKvvTh361R6jo0o/xGJk9vcs85RV/r9So6GZqFZPdzwYzyRz5tu6Vgkp5/s\nsG3yyUSc9zpblNULm99dLSopbLi2hSkV/jhhXOm47BcfyQjvL/ocwmvIR1Cr4Upo\nmdVslgS4uHzbk2mLfwIMnSaz+eUJQ2AB/JwZSFboZ8qvpPHgiSuNPfMufAFxOlmY\nh5AA99BRYfe7ZX537tVI1gPnhBamxTAW8iRVIjqDlmid/VFQ4rY45ngCDZPa3Gx8\n/P8AtyIimUlG8o1v8JNwlOuXRuASMlu8lbd9EG0AaN4azGHOKT7Ir8pf7QorqkNV\n5t9SnB8Kv8A3dMOoz20f/psNppPmt5jDPkqrM0QYa7qtvQOdGD/Zs3SPTRMDiSfT\n0nyN7R+jQxENI4nE1EZJbNiMmxdVmihBa1LSsBgKeI9aP1LChfaxtAq9QdbyIH7P\nvwx8YclAn8x/wTsvwQZOYmeYT9R4FsXCgoQUau/IItBpYWF8vqHSGnyX5VIYcjGq\nrtWGEdgKJzAX51wyrSQT7/C2a6iBDne9ZyWwvpsJXvc8du4kaowd+abGxJ1cQqDC\noV0CB9xSgTbAlf/TD63cyoOhR0Obur9f/dfslwYDzFVE3gDUewkEnNPqPBIngMQO\nwyjkEpoG3UPWV9s+LoRo\n=puXk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_