/api.github.com/users/keesverruijt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keesverruijt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keesverruijt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keesverruijt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/94ec5ed8d01a2c5d38803b2afc66351be2b3d4e0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T11:51:45Z","email":"kees@verruijt.net","name":"Kees Verruijt"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T11:51:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(container): keep radar settings across container recreates (#116)\n\nmayara stores its per-radar settings -- user-given name, guard zones,\nexclusion zones, range units, ARPA settings -- in settings.json under its\nconfig directory. The container declared no mount for it, so that file\nlived only in the writable layer, and signalk-container removes and\nrecreates the container on drift. With autoUpdateOnFloatingTag every new\n:latest digest therefore reset the user''s radar setup, unprompted.\n\nsignalkDataMount resolves the host-side source itself, so it works both\nbare-metal and when Signal K runs in its own container -- a plain volumes\nbind of getDataDirPath() would break in the latter. The mount lands on a\nsubdirectory rather than mayara''s config dir itself, keeping it clear of\nthe Signal K device token and cached GitHub token that also live there.\n\nCloses #111","tree":{"sha":"1d7a375f0d8973a49c11615059c2f606951bb638","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/trees/1d7a375f0d8973a49c11615059c2f606951bb638"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/commits/94ec5ed8d01a2c5d38803b2afc66351be2b3d4e0","verification":{"payload":"tree 1d7a375f0d8973a49c11615059c2f606951bb638\nparent 8f67a444b8f3555079082e6683ab63042b04ba01\nauthor Kees Verruijt <kees@verruijt.net> 1788004305 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788004305 +0900\n\nfix(container): keep radar settings across container recreates (#116)\n\nmayara stores its per-radar settings -- user-given name, guard zones,\nexclusion zones, range units, ARPA settings -- in settings.json under its\nconfig directory. The container declared no mount for it, so that file\nlived only in the writable layer, and signalk-container removes and\nrecreates the container on drift. With autoUpdateOnFloatingTag every new\n:latest digest therefore reset the user''s radar setup, unprompted.\n\nsignalkDataMount resolves the host-side source itself, so it works both\nbare-metal and when Signal K runs in its own container -- a plain volumes\nbind of getDataDirPath() would break in the latter. The mount lands on a\nsubdirectory rather than mayara''s config dir itself, keeping it clear of\nthe Signal K device token and cached GitHub token that also live there.\n\nCloses #111","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqksfRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5OsQABj37wUgdouuNDH5+dpsNhVL\n9EPg/8WL0IY68eY/eSj56Blcw+EaA8PidoTab3CbYI1x5RAOnh78Tva9IAPvBSRh\nE9AN5zNi0XXmwTjBddlIGiHSGDyUafC8L7gxpDlW74v2EU2ffvcOiP5k0WcsKEU0\nPcPpsXuejBnH6Pnu+kzsGfa1q5HZPuHGJ7J4SPkCLFJ1c4hjtxwchl3qa8GIkNgR\nVbigzcn2DgL8LKGW5/0ZvdWxCE791sS23SDRAc/d2lFm3DK3nxOtLND8yndp2CW6\nzzUjroC/3FWk4eFaBGWv4NkqtmK9Agv//Cy4XtDrvnxQh0lYIwez0b7c/yjKv6Rd\noMGNCesYLuGnZ5ixQmrfaIWtIl3c4KOv3Rg34PoEeQNEE8vNhSl80w+pZYJRMZHR\nQfkKtX9YOH67Zb68iP8yOBb6le7jL6qw6sprL8zI3lX+VqWNdaA82nvd76SNTcsy\nEiM1baDXHyL5giCYhAih48YnAKlV3YXw2uJqDcoYeSr7ad+JjFpqmHDQrHkFQDQd\ngwHEB82YpnYXg+Pz20knGbY3P6uECMnyXePkFbJ5tLAGs9Vqw77JEMi9xlAzefdV\nZvyLGgTYcwHG41s2IAtjyPz8h4EEf+9BQEIdSYIcuxMbfiBCJ6HOepI3Z/c+IijU\nzWwyShyTsDvHmlhtMkyE\n=mKXz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-29T11:51:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/