s","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keesverruijt/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keesverruijt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keesverruijt/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keesverruijt","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/e51a5965f7d6fecd59285cf5f1479fc2f8462ea8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T06:45:41Z","email":"kees@verruijt.net","name":"Kees Verruijt"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T06:45:41Z","email":"kees@verruijt.net","name":"Kees Verruijt"},"message":"fix(radar): send compound control payloads to mayara unwrapped\n\nsetControl wrapped every payload in the Signal K `{ value }` envelope. That is\nright for a scalar, but a compound control — a guard zone or a no-transmit\nsector — arrives as the body mayara already expects, so wrapping produced\n`{ value: { enabled: …, endValue: …, startDistance: … } }` and mayara answered\n400 \"Cannot control ''guardZone2'' to value {…}\". Zones and sectors could not be\nset through the plugin at all.\n\nWrap only a scalar; pass an object through as-is.\n\nThis is the plugin half of the fix. SignalK/signalk-server#2935 covers the\nother half: the Radar API discarded the sibling fields before the provider was\never called, so a zone PUT arrived here as a bare bearing and this bug stayed\nhidden behind that one.","tree":{"sha":"0e171339f7cbeb20756de80be0f9246357db57a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/trees/0e171339f7cbeb20756de80be0f9246357db57a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/commits/e51a5965f7d6fecd59285cf5f1479fc2f8462ea8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githu