/api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/45969bf0eb6d9261d90e2dd604fdebd1efe78fb2","node_id":"C_kwDOQqtUNdoAKDQ1OTY5YmYwZWI2ZDkyNjFkOTBlMmRkNjA0ZmRlYmQxZWZlNzhmYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/252645c2b6b716e3da215480a3e4336430aee55f","sha":"252645c2b6b716e3da215480a3e4336430aee55f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/252645c2b6b716e3da215480a3e4336430aee55f"}],"sha":"45969bf0eb6d9261d90e2dd604fdebd1efe78fb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/45969bf0eb6d9261d90e2dd604fdebd1efe78fb2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/252645c2b6b716e3da215480a3e4336430aee55f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T01:07:05Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T01:07:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(radar): report unknown state instead of a false ''off'' on a failed read (#101)\n\ngetState mapped power===2 to transmit, power===1 to standby, and *everything\nelse* to ''off''. That else swallowed the failure cases: a missing power control,\na transiently failed fetch, a 401 from an expired session. The plugin then\nasserted the radar was powered down when only the read had failed.\n\nThis actively misleads. An operator watching a transmitting radar flip to\n\"Off\" concludes the radar died, and goes looking at the radar instead of the\nconnection — it cost two rounds of misdiagnosis on a live boat before the logs\nshowed the radar transmitting happily throughout.\n\nUnusable readings now return null, which surfaces as unknown rather than as a\nconfident state the plugin cannot substantiate.\n\nThe same else also hid two real states. mayara''s power control declares five\nvalues (0 Off, 1 Standby, 2 Transmit, 3 Preparing, 4 Fault), so Preparing —\nthe magnetron warm-up, which the Radar API calls ''warming'' — was reported as\n''off'' for its whole duration, as was Fault. They are now mapped explicitly.\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"4fa62850050b237e433022ef1540474c9801eeba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/trees/4fa62850050b237e433022ef1540474c9801eeba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/commits/252645c2b6b716e3da215480a3e4336430aee55f","verification":{"payload":"tree 4fa62850050b237e433022ef1540474c9801eeba\nparent c8fdb9c76ec439712769ddc5ad1bec4ef89894e1\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1786237625 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786237625 +1200\n\nfix(radar): report unknown state instead of a false ''off'' on a failed read (#101)\n\ngetState mapped power===2 to transmit, power===1 to standby, and *everything\nelse* to ''off''. That else swallowed the failure cases: a missing power control,\na transiently failed fetch, a 401 from an expired session. The plugin then\nasserted the radar was powered down when only the read had failed.\n\nThis actively misleads. An operator watching a transmitting radar flip to\n\"Off\" concludes the radar died, and goes looking at the radar instead of the\nconnection — it cost two rounds of misdiagnosis on a live boat before the logs\nshowed the radar transmitting happily throughout.\n\nUnusable readings now return null, which surfaces as unknown rather than as a\nconfident state the plugin cannot substantiate.\n\nThe same else also hid two real states. mayara''s power control declares five\nvalues (0 Off, 1 Standby, 2 Transmit, 3 Preparing, 4 Fault), so Preparing —\nthe magnetron warm-up, which the Radar API calls ''warming'' — was reported as\n''off'' for its whole duration, as was Fault. They are now mapped explicitly.\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqd9K5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAK5AQAIjB4I4Vds6DW9vg0yM61Kjl\nf1MzPyaou/UjRpwrRqFGUYoXLmZoPetZzHX8jDHHfzX4eMz1k2SiqmpWYbxwEeGE\nVXioAaRhjeUQTH/5QNAfGh/RNvuf/zsAE46NezMCpp7mDLIQL+/flC0jEFP5oACZ\nkuydfXiUPZNjzIMOjP9mk5Qoy7H9N32dgKDIgSRUAF1jm5d96phwniBPUVN0A0t/\nParEtYxMxfbSx2G7JHpQ4yQf2f93IRt6kN3RQLnxWOa/IJeFUW7A0jaVMoPqPy7X\nzWQX5MpSAZwfWemb3npsGGAS1MvbjTwnVb45sOzh1q1CzzkHTp4TNes2MpUyr/K8\nhEkjrHu5dey3c4ZE0N6Q9UwyCPif+vtgF9MbjU/EKVsFxqnbYjP4bcNpkjb3VhiI\nvxH+4unEyFNgF7peOAuNLKU/UsAFBQGlnK/YNW8b+GIxnTPwyxDEsJsuDSdpSaOE\nUg1CWwK7OtNqh3FftH57YQCJ9jkJX5QsUAk8bV5L1jx3axLzgqgJ6/4rMKoj3JT5\nSQQFzC0NW5/317CN2MPSz4URHuAIFNBjrqpN8IV3St2tUYpjLphwYCPeu5h0g4h1\neZ/DlhvQq