/github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/b530d3eb56266257087336a41d18a7cd24d9ad9b","sha":"b530d3eb56266257087336a41d18a7cd24d9ad9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/b530d3eb56266257087336a41d18a7cd24d9ad9b"}],"sha":"c8fdb9c76ec439712769ddc5ad1bec4ef89894e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/c8fdb9c76ec439712769ddc5ad1bec4ef89894e1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/b530d3eb56266257087336a41d18a7cd24d9ad9b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T21:18:30Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T21:18:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(container): use signalk-container-helper for manager access and types (#99)\n\nReplaces three hand-rolled pieces with the shared library:\n\n- `waitForContainerManager` — the helper''s version distinguishes \"signalk-\n  container absent\" from \"present but no usable podman/docker\", which are\n  different operator problems; ours collapsed both into undefined and reported\n  the misleading first message.\n- `getContainerManager` — delegates, so the \"where does the manager live\"\n  knowledge lives in one place.\n- `SAFE_TAG` — the helper exports the same validation as `isValidImageTag`.\n\nThe bigger win is src/types.ts: 216 lines to 37. It hand-mirrored\nsignalk-container''s manager contract because a compile-time dependency on\nsignalk-container was impractical (its prerelease versioning breaks npm semver\nranges). signalk-container-helper solves that properly, so the mirror is gone\nand those types can no longer drift from the real API.\n\nTwo behavioural notes:\n\n- The helper skips whenReady() when getRuntime() already resolves, since\n  detection has by definition settled. The existing test asserted the *call*\n  rather than the invariant, so it now asserts that detection settled before\n  ensureRunning, and a new test covers the cold-boot path where getRuntime()\n  is null and whenReady() genuinely is awaited.\n- unbound-method is switched off for test/: mock assertions on vi.fn() stubs\n  cannot lose a this-binding, and the rule only started firing once the\n  helper''s typed interfaces replaced the loose local mirror.\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"65c3264fb388cc7d5a884614b7cb5795e5528cfa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/trees/65c3264fb388cc7d5a884614b7cb5795e5528cfa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/commits/b530d3eb56266257087336a41d18a7cd24d9ad9b","verification":{"payload":"tree 65c3264fb388cc7d5a884614b7cb5795e5528cfa\nparent 9696e675b8df7231205347b5e8c992a86eaccc6e\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1786223910 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786223910 +1200\n\nrefactor(container): use signalk-container-helper for manager access and types (#99)\n\nReplaces three hand-rolled pieces with the shared library:\n\n- `waitForContainerManager` — the helper''s version distinguishes \"signalk-\n  container absent\" from \"present but no usable podman/docker\", which are\n  different operator problems; ours collapsed both into undefined and reported\n  the misleading first message.\n- `getContainerManager` — delegates, so the \"where does the manager live\"\n  knowledge lives in one place.\n- `SAFE_TAG` — the helper exports the same validation as `isValidImageTag`.\n\nThe bigger win is src/types.ts: 216 lines to 37. It hand-mirrored\nsignalk-container''s manager contract because a compile-time dependency on\nsignalk-container was impractical (its prerelease versioning breaks npm semver\nranges). signalk-container-helper solves that properly, so the mirror is gone\nand those types can no longer drift from the real API.\n\nTwo behavioural notes:\n\n- The helper skips whenReady() when getRuntime() already resolves, since\n  detection has by definition settled. The existing test asserted the *call*\n  rather than the invariant, so it now asserts that detection settled before\n  ensureRunning, and a new test covers the cold-boot path where getRuntime()\n  is null and whenReady() genuinely is awaited.\n- unbound-method is switched off for test/: mock assertions on vi.fn() stubs\n  cannot lose a this-binding, and the rule only started firing once the\n  helper''s typed interfaces replaced the loose local mirror.\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqd50mCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAl2QQABi+IGKwGP6J2KEIj0eJRhuN\nf65K6hRFTU/zYDz4+q3hhDyj3SICIJSNRojpt9s/Qv89fFUVCp79pRpiMDrpPQXr\nQoBkLT07jWbK/OvagX0EOl+KwCAriuSuTz5Bu4z9wSRq64xGAGiC+sVr6wkAK1L4\n5XkfUjU1WDXZ5V5AzUSa9/LBOcVuhQGry1CFUv4rYPyBWPTUvO3zdxSGyj12odG2\nMv6KIlFx/ZXSdqtk504yJR/PkgW5hraKh9fYZe5e3tgb8nbaj8x8nl080aEQ4AV