,"site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/fd11fe321c8270dc1a83ee2e9b84db46cd27c63b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T18:45:44Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T18:45:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(deps): migrate to typebox 1.x (#93)\n\nTypeBox 1.x ships as the unscoped `typebox` package; `@sinclair/typebox` is a\ndifferent package name, frozen at 0.34.x. It is ESM-only — its exports map has\nno `require` condition — so this move was blocked until the plugin became ESM.\n\nThe API is unchanged: `Type.Object`/`String`/`Number`/`Boolean`/`Array` and\n`Static` all behave as before. The emitted JSON Schema is semantically\nidentical — same 9 properties, same required list, same defaults, titles,\ndescriptions and min/max bounds; only key order within each property differs\n(`type` now serialises first), which JSON Schema does not treat as meaningful.\nThat matters because Signal K renders the Admin UI form directly from this\nschema.\n\n`@sinclair/typebox` may still appear in node_modules: it arrives transitively\nvia @signalk/server-api, and is no longer a direct dependency.\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"d431e121db1dfee7f22207caa92b0b8a590391eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/trees/d431e121db1dfee7f22207caa92b0b8a590391eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/commits/fd11fe321c8270dc1a83ee2e9b84db46cd27c63b","verification":{"payload":"tree d431e121db1dfee7f22207caa92b0b8a590391eb\nparent 5a7242198fea7730491981d6fe72f2c0c8931e34\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1786214744 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786214744 +1200\n\nchore(deps): migrate to typebox 1.x (#93)\n\nTypeBox 1.x ships as the unscoped `typebox` package; `@sinclair/typebox` is a\ndifferent package name, frozen at 0.34.x. It is ESM-only — its exports map has\nno `require` condition — so this move was blocked until the plugin became ESM.\n\nThe API is unchanged: `Type.Object`/`String`/`Number`/`Boolean`/`Array` and\n`Static` all behave as before. The emitted JSON Schema is semantically\nidentical — same 9 properties, same required list, same defaults, titles,\ndescriptions and min/max bounds; only key order within each property differs\n(`type` now serialises first), which JSON Schema does not treat as meaningful.\nThat matters because Signal K renders the Admin UI form directly from this\nschema.\n\n`@sinclair/typebox` may still appear in node_modules: it arrives transitively\nvia @signalk/server-api, and is no longer a direct dependency.\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqd3lYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkgQQAJy+d6g8x3CwYpQCBAu8CCCd\nN2M+gKGndsgpkFN5sAGS8KG7Ln4Ta/r9y5nvD+RHQXmFs6M9CJVUiGOr8NcabPJs\nQW/5vdxMW28xnlZl60Evp3g0L7szwlgsdwk9dtsy+Xv+PGi22OIubH+CgCSzclpx\nsZ+6TI1CjdlOjW6cUVOZCIU0jOywcNDi325Zr5NSCrt+ZOf5+JECFueJ3RuhDSD8\nQjMo9HBz+FQntYjjlZRV5KVJGUzG1x9d5/C3dHki4GDKKp2UB+w3KbnHUq/qZNiA\n1pB1fPQEnlGxcMF23z5/MwWM08/KrLaRmEDoeeej/xMhIfQWBWGnRuzSnU5Q3e1S\ncS3+svsVz8L6xXpdyYMK3r5x0FXmk+WJPPVOlop7ZdmL7T7KuESkG65oeHQsV7q/\n3I33IA0+fZApsvFkGOVm1YnCF3gIX4ES80/ltd09AT3DH0bsPFc0FXFfu2iqeDuS\nNPHSafWWY75bRo3q4nBUw0eQgTpMtIMU9yxFiyFvrp9b7HIjiYqabPA+yPYgtN7y\nu08LDh8GK7721OLpvfFyE2CWwgl26+B05zYXBnIWab5H7vnxku7sVkVRuNBxaqeh\n27MD4kKmSWb2uECcafJaxPWB9jk/YEAjmmzGYyw0katc4pwIMZs5kRDxmWWgtiq3\nYKis6egFAYqqmqKtBgTP\n=4kwi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-08T18:47:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/fd11fe321c8270dc1a83ee2e9b84db46cd27c63b","node_id":"C_kwDOQqtUNdoAKGZkMTFmZTMyMWM4MjcwZGMxYTgzZWUyZTliODRkYjQ2Y2QyN2M2M2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/5a7242198fea7730491981d6fe72f2c0c8931e34","sha":"5a7242198fea7730491981d6fe72f2c0c8931e34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/5a7242198fea7730491981d6fe72f2c0c8931e34"}],"sha":"fd11fe321c8270dc1a83ee2e9b84db46cd27c63b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/fd11fe321c8270dc1a83ee2e9b84db46cd27c63b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/5a7242198fea7730491981d6fe72f2c0c8931e34/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T18:27:28Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T18:27:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(configpanel): convert the config panel to strict TypeScript (#92)\n\n* refactor(configpanel): convert the config panel to strict TypeScript\n\nThe panel was the last untyped code in the repo: ~670 lines of .js/.jsx that\ntsc never compiled and eslint.config.mjs explicitly ignored. It stayed that\nway because babel-loader only resolved .js/.jsx; Vite compiles .tsx natively,\nso that constraint is gone. eslint now points the type-aware parser at the\npanel''s own tsconfig, so it is linted under the same strictTypeChecked rules\nas the rest of src/.\n\nversionsView.d.ts is deleted rather than updated — it was a hand-maintained\nshim over versionsView.js that could silently drift from the implementation\nit described. The types now come from the implementation.\n\nDropping the eslint ignore surfaced 322 problems. Most were formatting, but\nthe substantive ones were real: Response.json() is typed `any`, which spread\nuntyped values through every derived state and status string. Reads now go\nthrough readJson() returning `unknown`, and each payload is validated at the\ncall site — /status in particular, since `radars.length` and the string-split\nof `container.image` would throw on a malformed body. Floating promises in\nthe mount effect and async onClick handlers are marked `void`, and a dead\nupdateAvailable computation (never rendered, pre-existing) is removed.\n\nFixes the three panel issues raised while reviewing the Vite migration and\ndeferred there, since that PR only renamed the file:\n\n- CollapsibleSection''s header was a click-handled <div>, unreachable by\n  keyboard and silent to assistive tech; it is now a <button aria-expanded>.\n- Form controls were labelled by adjacent <span>s with no association; they\n  now use <label htmlFor> against unique control ids.\n- The numeric inputs coerced with Number() on every keystroke, so clearing\n  the port box wrote 0 (Number('''') === 0) and a partial entry became NaN.\n  SCHEMA_DEFAULTS only fills missing keys, so an explicit 0 would persist.\n  They keep raw input while editing and are range-checked as whole numbers\n  in doSave().\n\nFurther review fixes: every button sets type=\"button\" rather than defaulting\nto submit; formatTimeAgo tests the parsed date instead of relying on a\ntry/catch that cannot fire (an unparseable date yields NaN, which rendered as\n\"NaNd ago\"); and deriveVersionsView drops entries whose tag is missing or\nblank and ignores undocumented source statuses, since a blank tag rendered an\nempty <option> that could be saved as the image tag.\n\n* fix(configpanel): parse image tags after the last colon, tighten types and a11y\n\nFrom the review of #92:\n\n- The running tag was read with image.split('':'')[1], which returns the\n  registry port on a reference like registry.example.com:5000/mayara:latest.\n  Both call sites now use a shared imageTag() that reads the segment after the\n  last colon and rejects one containing ''/''. The value is persisted by doSave\n  and sent as the requested tag by doUpdate, so a wrong parse was not cosmetic.\n- engines.node is >=22.15.0: http-proxy-middleware v4 requires ^22.15.0, and\n  the previous >=22 would have let npm install it on a Node it cannot run on.\n  README updated to match; the major is unchanged, so @types/node ^22 and the\n  dependabot pin still hold.\n- The update-check payload is decoded field by field rather than cast, so a\n  server sending an object for `error` can no longer render\n  \"Check failed: [object Object]\".\n- The style map uses `satisfies` instead of a Record annotation, so a\n  mistyped key fails the build rather than silently rendering unstyled.\n- Accessibility: the refresh button gets an aria-label (it renders only a\n  glyph, and title is not reliably announced), and each radar card states\n  streaming/connecting as text rather than by dot colour alone.\n- Relative imports in the panel carry .js, matching the specifier the test\n  already uses.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"d1f74c1b033a5f1ae1f0cf9cdfab1f7a64dab1eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/trees/d1f74c1b033a5f1ae1f0cf9cdfab1f7a64dab1eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/commits/5a7242198fea7730491981d6fe72f2c0c8931e34","verification":{"payload":"tree d1f74c1b033a5f1ae1f0cf9cdfab1f7a64dab1eb\nparent 203ad425e63b2dbe4b8c708ce4d358e7541a642e\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1786213648 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786213648 +1200\n\nrefactor(configpanel): convert the config panel to strict TypeScript (#92)\n\n* refactor(configpanel): convert the config panel to strict TypeScript\n\nThe panel was the last untyped code in the repo: ~670 lines of .js/.jsx that\ntsc never compiled and eslint.config.mjs explicitly ignored. It stayed that\nway because babel-loader only resolved .js/.jsx; Vite compiles .tsx natively,\nso that constraint is gone. eslint now points the type-aware parser at the\npanel''s own tsconfig, so it is linted under the same strictTypeChecked rules\nas the rest of src/.\n\nversionsView.d.ts is deleted rather than updated — it was a hand-maintained\nshim over versionsView.js that could silently drift from the implementation\nit described. The types now come from the implementation.\n\nDropping the eslint ignore surfaced 322 problems. Most were formatting, but\nthe substantive ones were real: Response.json() is typed `any`, which spread\nuntyped values through every derived state and status string. Reads now go\nthrough readJson() returning `unknown`, and each payload is validated at the\ncall site — /status in particular, since `radars.length` and the string-split\nof `container.image` would throw on a malformed body. Floating promises in\nthe mount effect and async onClick handlers are marked `void`, and a dead\nupdateAvailable computation (never rendered, pre-existing) is removed.\n\nFixes the three panel issues raised while reviewing the Vite migration and\ndeferred there, since that PR only renamed the file:\n\n- CollapsibleSection''s header was a click-handled <div>, unreachable by\n  keyboard and silent to assistive tech; it is now a <button aria-expanded>.\n- Form controls were labelled by adjacent <span>s with no association; they\n  now use <label htmlFor> against unique control ids.\n- The numeric inputs coerced with Number() on every keystroke, so clearing\n  the port box wrote 0 (Number('''') === 0) and a partial entry became NaN.\n  SCHEMA_DEFAULTS only fills missing keys, so an explicit 0 would persist.\n  They keep raw input while editing and are range-checked as whole numbers\n  in doSave().\n\nFurther review fixes: every button sets type=\"button\" rather than defaulting\nto submit; formatTimeAgo tests the parsed date instead of relying on a\ntry/catch that cannot fire (an unparseable date yields NaN, which rendered as\n\"NaNd ago\"); and deriveVersionsView drops entries whose tag is missing or\nblank and ignores undocumented source statuses, since a blank tag rendered an\nempty <option> that could be saved as the image tag.\n\n* fix(configpanel): parse image tags after the last colon, tighten types and a11y\n\nFrom the review of #92:\n\n- The running tag was read with image.split('':'')[1], which returns the\n  registry port on a reference like registry.example.com:5000/mayara:latest.\n  Both call sites now use a shared imageTag() that reads the segment after the\n  last colon and rejects one containing ''/''. The value is persisted by doSave\n  and sent as the requested tag by doUpdate, so a wrong parse was not cosmetic.\n- engines.node is >=22.15.0: http-proxy-middleware v4 requires ^22.15.0, and\n  the previous >=22 would have let npm install it on a Node it cannot run on.\n  README updated to match; the major is unchanged, so @types/node ^22 and the\n  dependabot pin still hold.\n- The update-check payload is decoded field by field rather than cast, so a\n  server sending an object for `error` can no longer render\n  \"Check failed: [object Object]\".\n- The style map uses `satisfies` instead of a Record annotation, so a\n  mistyped key fails the build rather than silently rendering unstyled.\n- Accessibility: the refresh button gets an aria-label (it renders only a\n  glyph, and title is not reliably announced), and each radar card states\n  streaming/connecting as text rather than by dot colour alone.\n- Relative imports in the panel carry .js, matching the specifier the test\n  already uses.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqd3UQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAgQQAFrPFZ2CXC0zmR0pToWhp6Au\nBSdXB7rYA6FoL6iVmiy10xcxspS8W4GyqapY770J+TrL+MwogBiZfBU8zH7L/vNq\n2W7s8XJniBi7zARsBaBXv1XvBsZJHu+2pZXnYRxTYtVNb+SX/zRPJxA+4S81Ju1J\ngCAiH66HXO2DbJbMtQHPyXGL/hnblyFq9UO3KUSq0+sAk1gqtq556bL+IR