pi.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/4717f57682fd1047a7813e41db0c7d3d2d3d9c10","node_id":"C_kwDOQqtUNdoAKDQ3MTdmNTc2ODJmZDEwNDdhNzgxM2U0MWRiMGM3ZDNkMmQzZDljMTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/bb97cfae6ca99c40c6874a01b7626df4ff26b9f8","sha":"bb97cfae6ca99c40c6874a01b7626df4ff26b9f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/bb97cfae6ca99c40c6874a01b7626df4ff26b9f8"}],"sha":"4717f57682fd1047a7813e41db0c7d3d2d3d9c10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/4717f57682fd1047a7813e41db0c7d3d2d3d9c10"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/bb97cfae6ca99c40c6874a01b7626df4ff26b9f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-04T16:40:45Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-04T16:40:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(versions): authenticate GitHub calls and surface rate-limit failures (#84)\n\n* fix(versions): authenticate GitHub calls and surface rate-limit failures\n\nThe config panel''s version dropdown lost its PR test images, and the\n\"Check\" button failed with \"GitHub API 429\", when GitHub rate-limited the\nplugin''s unauthenticated REST calls. A boat sharing a WAN IP with other\nGitHub-polling plugins exhausts the 60-req/hr unauthenticated limit (and\ntrips GitHub''s stickier 429 secondary limit), so both the dropdown''s\n/api/versions calls and signalk-container''s update-check source returned\nerrors and the images vanished.\n\nRead an optional GitHub token (GITHUB_TOKEN | GH_TOKEN env, or a\ngithub-token file in the plugin data dir) and pass it to both GitHub\npaths: the /api/versions releases+pulls fetches and the githubReleases\nupdate source registered with signalk-container. A token lifts the limit\nto 5000/hr, curing the exhaustion. The token is optional and not a\nuser-facing config field; absent, the calls stay unauthenticated with no\nregression. It lives in signalk-token.ts because the repo forbids fs\nimports in index.ts. A present-but-rejected token (401) retries once\nunauthenticated, so a bad token is never worse than none.\n\nStop silently blanking the PR images on a rate-limit: /api/versions now\nreturns {versions, sources} with each source classified ok / rate-limited\n/ error (reading the rate-limit response headers), and the panel shows a\ndedicated line distinguishing \"rate-limited, retry shortly\" from a\ngeneric fetch error, so the operator can tell that from \"no PR images\nexist\". A running pr<N> whose fetch was rate-limited keeps a synthetic\n\"(running)\" dropdown option instead of blank-resetting the selection.\n\n* fix(versions): treat Retry-After as rate-limited and share tag classification\n\nAddress review feedback on the GitHub resilience change:\n\n- classify() now also returns rate-limited when a 403/429 carries a\n  Retry-After header, not only when x-ratelimit-remaining is 0. GitHub''s\n  secondary/abuse limit — the one a shared WAN IP trips — sends\n  Retry-After without remaining:0, so it was being misreported as a\n  generic error and the panel told the operator \"retry\" was not possible.\n- Extract splitVersions() as the single source of the dropdown''s\n  slice limits; shownTags and the panel''s optgroup builder both consume\n  it, so runningTagFallback can no longer drift from the rendered option\n  list.\n- Rename the fetch result in ghFetch from res to ghRes so it no longer\n  shadows the Express response object.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"b4c123182609cf74317b225c30e15d8a4a7d949e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/trees/b4c123182609cf74317b225c30e15d8a4a7d949e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/commits/bb97cfae6ca99c40c6874a01b7626df4ff26b9f8","verification":{"payload":"tree b4c123182609cf74317b225c30e15d8a4a7d949e\nparent 4f6190e506ddc8966002f6caf6b02c48420d1656\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1783183245 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783183245 +1200\n\nfix(versions): authenticate GitHub calls and surface rate-limit failures (#84)\n\n* fix(versions): authenticate GitHub calls and surface rate-limit failures\n\nThe config panel''s version dropdown lost its PR test images, and the\n\"Check\" button failed with \"GitHub API 429\", when GitHub rate-limited the\nplugin''s unauthenticated REST calls. A boat sharing a WAN IP with other\nGitHub-polling plugins exhausts the 60-req/hr unauthenticated limit (and\ntrips GitHub''s stickier 429 secondary limit), so both the dropdown''s\n/api/versions calls and signalk-container''s update-check source returned\nerrors and the images vanished.\n\nRead an optional GitHub token (GITHUB_TOKEN | GH_TOKEN env, or a\ngithub-token file in the plugin data dir) and pass it to both GitHub\npaths: the /api/versions releases+pulls fetches and the githubReleases\nupdate source registered with signalk-container. A token lifts the limit\nto 5000/hr, curing the exhaustion. The token is optional and not a\nuser-facing config field; absent, the calls stay unauthenticated with no\nregression. It lives in signalk-token.ts because the repo forbids fs\nimports in index.ts. A present-but-rejected token (401) retries once\nunauthenticated, so a bad token is never worse than none.\n\nStop silently blanking the PR images on a rate-limit: /api/versions now\nreturns {versions, sources} with each source classified ok / rate-limited\n/ error (reading the rate-limit response headers), and the panel shows a\ndedicated line distinguishing \"rate-limited, retry shortly\" from a\ngeneric fetch error, so the operator can tell that from \"no PR images\nexist\". A running pr<N> whose fetch was rate-limited keeps a synthetic\n\"(running)\" dropdown option instead of blank-resetting the selection.\n\n* fix(versions): treat Retry-After as rate-limited and share tag classification\n\nAddress review feedback on the GitHub resilience change:\n\n- classify() now also returns rate-limited when a 403/429 carries a\n  Retry-After header, not only when x-ratelimit-remaining is 0. GitHub''s\n  secondary/abuse limit — the one a shared WAN IP trips — sends\n  Retry-After without remaining:0, so it was being misreported as a\n  generic error and the panel told the operator \"retry\" was not possible.\n- Extract splitVersions() as the single source of the dropdown''s\n  slice limits; shownTags and the panel''s optgroup builder both consume\n  it, so runningTagFallback can no longer drift from the rendered option\n  list.\n- Rename the fetch result in ghFetch from res to ghRes so it no longer\n  shadows the Express response object.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqSTeNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAutQQAI9zwZ8Y39d/2+kis7LoPlJJ\nLPyOUc+X3mh1u8Vi5heo3SCjHt/NVDntDd8fvN7RXQherfrEmDFPbrF0X3ib65e2\nBCCh0DtEiYmuCCww+UvYnTbKuMXHg+YNFXMM0FNwclfK15ydCDl+xxhjzYorbWP6\nCB6kDcYBZmDGpVURdfAjfnHV6HhRy7UueNOTN455loed7GyTnPcZLxMuvqp6UDHT\nUNCDUJC/HzBnpAsSN17YsEUgM5+hUF4GrbEj4AdO87MkrmGaGbW+Hepo44qg29/+\n+IoFn5IhGYCNomWZ88na66a/e2DiIFhL+f+zYVims98wJXYh5ipyOt5jeoX1VLIC\nGhZ6krTZMCqUJJEnTXzE/zX45vGHPaC5XrPFlqHwJFVD4Gy0TtEvXh60u7dYuJLv\nLD+xX6Ln1I8c9YhXJjItWysgrpFmmREKVHz9LKbUfXDPc9MwcI+byaxFKdLPtODA\n+qLWpYx9ARdhsul1iRiZ6Phx16VSoeBBoWpXWIiacLA3PqMoYMZm1zxx1YKF9ra2\naNRE5evBZp470m+HKhpNHSoSOwfQfO8mqiKQhQLG/omXg0VK3PUdnGlBih+nR4eH\nx5nrdX0pO8e0jvPNbbtXhg+0hpsvl062AIW3f2OksbggfDz8lmr4UlftBUZ3c72s\n2vaKamBf3CGMdx8eJ1U/\n=uxDE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-04T16:40:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/othe