71be7bb3acb5051f1e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/e381b984f00a7d277e278f10b687882222d3e31d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T23:30:24Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T23:30:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: refurbish AGENTS.md for current architecture and radar status model (#74)\n\nThe previous guidance predated the current src/ module split and carried\nframing inherited from the Signal K template. Refresh the architecture map\nto today''s modules and add a Radar status model section capturing the\ntwo-axis design (lifecycle status vs idle), the never-silently-drop-a-radar\nprinciple, the ARPA-is-a-subscriber rule, and the receiver_count/ARPA idle\ngotcha, so future agents build the status work correctly instead of\nre-introducing the unhealthy-radar kludge.\n\nAlso correct token-flow drift: document validate-on-start + re-request\nwithout restart, and fix a stale reference to a tokenPollerCancelled flag\nthat does not exist (the mechanism is the tokenGeneration counter).\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"04911ba994fc17993d00c54e84d09d5cd5051d01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/trees/04911ba994fc17993d00c54e84d09d5cd5051d01"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/commits/e381b984f00a7d277e278f10b687882222d3e31d","verification":{"payload":"tree 04911ba994fc17993d00c54e84d09d5cd5051d01\nparent 54833d25ba141896892d36d48e1d72a07f95a500\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1780615824 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780615824 +1200\n\ndocs: refurbish AGENTS.md for current architecture and radar status model (#74)\n\nThe previous guidance predated the current src/ module split and carried\nframing inherited from the Signal K template. Refresh the architecture map\nto today''s modules and add a Radar status model section capturing the\ntwo-axis design (lifecycle status vs idle), the never-silently-drop-a-radar\nprinciple, the ARPA-is-a-subscriber rule, and the receiver_count/ARPA idle\ngotcha, so future agents build the status work correctly instead of\nre-introducing the unhealthy-radar kludge.\n\nAlso correct token-flow drift: document validate-on-start + re-request\nwithout restart, and fix a stale reference to a tokenPollerCancelled flag\nthat does not exist (the mechanism is the tokenGeneration counter).\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIgqQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVx0QAD6BNbTDX9CNVGF/EbUUuOa7\nz27sBUu4PU0Z4kJ4pKXoH04Q7bvuCfAzrIxFWGLqZNX/ov30UkdLRyHqd0VMRJXJ\nKWBjazCRItFq857JP5Lr0I2+sPVAG3YXbUttZkVNLqkSAw0AupQiVjpvtjAIXDm2\nO23WRzkwRNV1il5CQqVYsS5wj9uOUKIWUOPr8n7XHZ4fRjOAG/8g3RryZBR4KhiM\nJ1oHR4peGRwBmvvVLiBMOe6wFDq0R9ImgKjLgKGAya8zW4FkQzDJm8M9b8pJ8rY0\n