"id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/d10fbad68cb7eac33c8a47fbd1327392ee875c7c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-02T00:52:02Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-02T00:52:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(token): detect a revoked cached token and re-request (#65)\n\nThe plugin trusted the on-disk Signal K token forever: once cached, start()\nreturned early without checking it. If the admin revoked it, mayara kept\nrunning with the dead token on its ws: upstream (rejected with 401), the AIS\nseed silently failed, and nothing recovered until a manual restart.\n\nValidate the cached token against the local SK on start; on 401/403 drop the\ncache, recreate the container (so it falls back to tcp: until re-approved),\nand re-request via the existing recovery loop. A network blip returns\n''unknown'' so a transient outage never throws away a good token.","tree":{"sha":"82e5f67818e133fedf55060eec3ba2442a583e0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/trees/82e5f67818e133fedf55060eec3ba2442a583e0c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/commits/d10fbad68cb7eac33c8a47fbd1327392ee875c7c","verification":{"payload":"tree 82e5f67818e133fedf55060eec3ba2442a583e0c\nparent 398e7520121278b42a8ceb5b861260d15d40852d\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1780361522 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780361522 +1200\n\nfix(token): detect a revoked cached token and re-request (#65)\n\nThe plugin trusted the on-disk Signal K token forever: once cached, start()\nreturned early without checking it. If the admin revoked it, mayara kept\nrunning with the dead token on its ws: upstream (rejected with 401), the AIS\nseed silently failed, and nothing recovered until a manual restart.\n\nValidate the cached token against the local SK on start; on 401/403 drop the\ncache, recreate the container (so it falls back to tcp: until re-approved),\nand re-request via the existing recovery loop. A network blip returns\n''unknown'' so a transient outage never throws away a good token.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHikyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZr0QAHE5aB10ft2laWfeWj3uQzKq\nEesWxynkgVTsj15BSKq2apsUhIYh7xuGqZj8MArl3BJXkvmW2qssLXM1jm1amVwP\nMYG1Qgovp/5+YRpI+m2+4+Ei9tbW1f0DSYPGJJr1YT+yPmO12wqaLANldxU9WSs+\njFjIUG076OPmTR9dbMl6SjFILBh21JPcZtTNB/BkQb/GR8HHYaKLH/sTja1ld+s5\nWuOnFGOREJRQqIrkFcoE+OQ7fpa+O99tpuDhYcPODBAZmXhjWxXa2LGLZO5aIK2J\nR2bpskE+ChoB8l/wnekydCwhYeCoU/Cn6u1bOgsU+GXrg0GGe4JIyvQM6D0EuhT2\nzcnFuqiVTPlaLwhx3l5hw/EDbQIhcD0ck/wu3I543ZIZWGLjc2DGekPyhEd8+S1O\nkHWmiEUhV4kX+XrLPP1238fHcXVNbEvK1VZLDyQkNdjEnfFudxZUExtuzaZ0nyYh\ncLpnn/vaW22hi3F7aai2f6LzUhJBvO0zYNuOxXRg4epchhr37FQaF+QRj86EZD+Y\n3QIx/lrq/zw43vPkyMqqf8LoJ/+phpM0DnY34C6m/Tlt91zNeKadxruL3D2g/oOV\nRijXfDxpb6NAGPep1FDEWsnS1Ek4RANSGaMbHl+vuDe5dyIdqioYW7nQmc+0u0DF\nINkqOj1iRF7S2p4woyYh\n=m5C/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-02T00:52:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/o