iptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/aa05bff5a8b0e92867e2d5b29e4ecae42131ed69","node_id":"C_kwDOQqtUNdoAKGFhMDViZmY1YThiMGU5Mjg2N2UyZDViMjllNGVjYWU0MjEzMWVkNjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commit/a4c06d0ba14bb95482b2f817358f0f13e901a650","sha":"a4c06d0ba14bb95482b2f817358f0f13e901a650","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/a4c06d0ba14bb95482b2f817358f0f13e901a650"}],"sha":"aa05bff5a8b0e92867e2d5b29e4ecae42131ed69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/aa05bff5a8b0e92867e2d5b29e4ecae42131ed69"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/commits/a4c06d0ba14bb95482b2f817358f0f13e901a650/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-31T23:43:29Z","email":"86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-31T23:43:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(status): surface \"update available\" in the plugin status line (#58)\n\n* feat(status): surface \"update available\" in the plugin status line\n\nWhen the managed container ran an outdated floating-tag image, nothing\ntold the operator — plugin status read \"Connected - N radars\" while a\nnewer image (with fixes) sat unused, so a stale container looked healthy\nand the only symptom was missing functionality.\n\nOn connect, run signalk-container''s offline-tolerant, cached update\ncheck and, when a newer image is available, append \"· update available\n(click Update)\" to the status line. Best-effort and non-blocking:\nfailures clear the hint and never delay startup. Managed mode only;\ncleared on a successful Update and on stop().\n\nAlso makes the test harness MayaraClient mock `new`-able (it returned an\narrow function, which threw \"is not a constructor\" and had silently\nprevented any connect-path coverage).\n\n* fix(status): refresh update hint after a late reconnect\n\nattemptReconnect reaches ''Connected'' without going through\nconnectAndDiscover, so the update-available hint was never computed when\na boot reached connected state via the reconnect loop (mayara not ready\nat startup). Run the same non-blocking refreshUpdateHint() there.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"fa11e4cae883559eaeed08e83e9b5fedf5ef3690","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/trees/fa11e4cae883559eaeed08e83e9b5fedf5ef3690"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarineYachtRadar/mayara-server-signalk-plugin/git/commits/a4c06d0ba14bb95482b2f817358f0f13e901a650","verification":{"payload":"tree fa11e4cae883559eaeed08e83e9b5fedf5ef3690\nparent f100ae4712ca0b214dca919b9f062156fcbfa8a7\nauthor Dirk Wahrheit <86628605+dirkwa@users.noreply.github.com> 1780271009 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780271009 +1200\n\nfeat(status): surface \"update available\" in the plugin status line (#58)\n\n* feat(status): surface \"update available\" in the plugin status line\n\nWhen the managed container ran an outdated floating-tag image, nothing\ntold the operator — plugin status read \"Connected - N radars\" while a\nnewer image (with fixes) sat unused, so a stale container looked healthy\nand the only symptom was missing functionality.\n\nOn connect, run signalk-container''s offline-tolerant, cached update\ncheck and, when a newer image is available, append \"· update available\n(click Update)\" to the status line. Best-effort and non-blocking:\nfailures clear the hint and never delay startup. Managed mode only;\ncleared on a successful Update and on stop().\n\nAlso makes the test harness MayaraClient mock `new`-able (it returned an\narrow function, which threw \"is not a constructor\" and had silently\nprevented any connect-path coverage).\n\n* fix(status): refresh update hint after a late reconnect\n\nattemptReconnect reaches ''Connected'' without going through\nconnectAndDiscover, so the update-available hint was never computed when\na boot reached connected state via the reconnect loop (mayara not ready\nat startup). Run the same non-blocking refreshUpdateHint() there.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: dirkwa <dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHMehCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA23IQAAm5SB5f+YK6ZKAowoSg3z2j\nzCPYIi/A11o20CWriPfloPAoIw0B6Fa6OGOQAM116hUB8oQRtDQ2G/5AfdLn8W10\npw/aYfJMRf6aQG8DnDAxZ9aOBMJWCGaP3enrAPRno2nIY2JxRBDOebqPHy34iffx\n4mtck5yjbQlh6uEjyXC5EOM1tKiMFjKMWsNgzgUwo1P0L+iXqmCfa0x8ar67TrLT\nrvA707xduQWflPaOhSYhFKIh1wZnKPCq6wf+B6ucpBZ0/i8g3XHkmqJL7Y0a46Qm\nWZde4RlAH6wI0ddtY02cQbBv5jzs1TC17hXskuxBMw2o2isz/XN5RU1gYLvXHeqt\nX6oqwCH62nbybO0uoWhrzIgkZPp9UjVpCDnAyzAaJ/VDOsRw+6MaE+JfBM6asaen\nhYy986WPzLROItNiW7zFRWcHBayx