Hash\n- Deterministic JSON serialization for hash chain\n- FNV-1a 32-bit fast hashing (no crypto dependencies)\n\n[12] Audit Log (Hash-Chain Journal)\n- GENESIS → hash-chained event entries\n- Every privileged action recorded with prev/hash\n- In-memory ring buffer (max 2048 entries)\n- Replayable kernel journal for verification\n\n[13] JavaCrypt Opcode Contract v1\n- Allowlisted ops: kernel.ping, audit.export, tape.put/get/list,\n  cluster.run/status, agent.spawn/list, research.search/fetch,\n  pi.emit/infer, host.probe, manifest.get/patch\n- Block validation: v, id, t, op, payload fields required\n- Silent changes eliminated (everything audited)\n\n[14] JavaCrypt Dispatch Table (Audited)\n- Each op handler with audit_event() calls\n- tape.put/get with size validation\n- agent.spawn/list via AgentBus\n- research.search via micro-agents\n\n[15] Research Agent Registry (AgentBus)\n- Micro-agents: router, wikipedia, github, rss\n- Per-agent metrics: calls, errors, lastMs\n- Agent audit log (separate from kernel audit)\n\n[16] Research Routes & Implementations\n- /research/agents - list registered agents\n- /research/audit - agent activity log\n- /research/search?q=...&n=... - fan-out search\n- Wikipedia OpenSearch API (CORS-friendly)\n- GitHub repository search API\n- PROXY mode for non-CORS sources\n\nSealed Message Bridge:\n- __javacrypt__: true blocks routed to opcode executor\n- Legacy mx2.* messages still supported for compatibility\n- All calls audited with client ID\n\nVersion bumped to 1.2.4","tree":{"sha":"2d0a4f9bc84cc3a0c54db20eceb2925091572897","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cannaseedus-bot/ASX-BROWSER/git/trees/2d0a4f9bc84cc3a0c54db20eceb2925091572897"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cannaseedus-bot/ASX-BROWSER/git/commits/7d4b8080725611ff4d17e829b5b37b3a23b78b20","verification":{"payload":"tree 2d0a4f9bc84cc3a0c54db20eceb2925091572897\nparent 245afce0b29495585442b130bebc2fa4cccce89d\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1766288349 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1766288349 +0000\n\nExtend K''UHUL π kernel with audit log, JavaCrypt v1, and research agents\n\nNEW SECTIONS ADDED:\n\n[11] Stable Stringify + FNV-1a Hash\n- Deterministic JSON serialization for hash chain\n- FNV-1a 32-bit fast hashing (no crypto dependencies)\n\n[12] Audit Log (Hash-Chain Journal)\n- GENESIS → hash-chained event entries\n- Every privileged action recorded with prev/hash\n- In-memory ring buffer (max 2048 entries)\n- Replayable kernel journal for verification\n\n[13] JavaCrypt Opcode Contract v1\n- Allowlisted ops: kernel.ping, audit.export, tape.put/get/list,\n  cluster.run/status, agent.spawn/list, research.search/fetch,\n  pi.emit/infer, host.probe, manifest.get/patch\n- Block validation: v, id, t, op, payload fields required\n- Silent changes eliminated (everything audited)\n\n[14] JavaCrypt Dispatch Table (Audited)\n- Each op handler with audit_event() calls\n- tape.put/get with size validation\n- agent.spawn/list via AgentBus\n- research.search via micro-agents\n\n[15] Research Agent Registry (AgentBus)\n- Micro-agents: router, wikipedia, github, rss\n- Per-agent metrics: calls, errors, lastMs\n- Agent audit log (separate from kernel audit)\n\n[16] Research Routes & Implementations\n- /research/agents - list registered agents\n- /research/audit - agent activity log\n- /research/search?q=...&n=... - fan-out search\n- Wikipedia OpenSearch API (CORS-friendly)\n- GitHub repository search API\n- PROXY mode for non-CORS sources\n\nSealed Message Bridge:\n- __javacrypt__: true blocks routed to opcode executor\n- Legacy mx2.* messages still supported for compatibility\n- All calls audited with client ID\n\nVersion bumped to 1.2.4\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOgDfVap\nwnbNJo4jtAauFY512VdqUyPSXCxau7Bt5+zLWD+Y1MQHq+BBsYyYk5O9VkJ+pK+pwEW9Bs