unreachable!()`/`panic!()` calls in the binding filter\nexpression normalization pipeline with `anyhow::Result` in\n`rolldown_utils` and `napi::Error` at the binding boundary. When users\nbypass TypeScript type checking and pass invalid filter payloads,\nrolldown now returns a clean error like `\"Invalid filter expression in\nplugin ''my-plugin'': expected a string or regex payload, but got\nNumber(42)\"` instead of crashing. Adds a JS test fixture to verify the\nbehavior.\n\nclosed https://github.com/rolldown/rolldown/issues/8661","tree":{"sha":"d378a9f2f14072688f43cff613039df3126aa511","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shulaoda/rolldown-with-module-federation-2.0/git/trees/d378a9f2f14072688f43cff613039df3126aa511"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shulaoda/rolldown-with-module-federation-2.0/git/commits/ae6b599cdf29a4041ef445b69fe60c6b57a6a800","verification":{"payload":"tree d378a9f2f14072688f43cff613039df3126aa511\nparent b15ec6078ef8a07ec40fa38b766d0bf9061fcde3\nauthor IWANABETHATGUY <iwanabethatguy@qq.com> 1773464965 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773464965 +0800\n\nfix: replace panics with proper errors in filter expression normalization\n (#8664)\n\n**Description:**\n\nReplace all `unreachable!()`/`panic!()` calls in the binding filter\nexpression normalization pipeline with `anyhow::Result` in\n`rolldown_utils` and `napi::Error` at the binding boundary. When users\nbypass TypeScript type checking and pass invalid filter payloads,\nrolldown now returns a clean error like `\"Invalid filter expression in\nplugin ''my-plugin'': expected a string or regex payload, but got\nNumber(42)\"` instead of crashing. Adds a JS test fixture to verify the\nbehavior.\n\nclosed https://github.com/rolldown/rolldown/issues/8661","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJptO2FCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOvkQAKv+rUfqDJRSQwfmaVR5IoC1\n3HOw6ARHsa4hk0FDb7OV7s06KTmbjIizKDdQDopTC0BmY277defH0SEv3gyCV8N2\nmpzpfTFRxbJX45HcmH6lD49bZrfVq1X6rbF1lJ