a/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonzylstra/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brandonzylstra","id":9854,"login":"brandonzylstra","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NTQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonzylstra/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonzylstra/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonzylstra/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonzylstra/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonzylstra/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brandonzylstra","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shulaoda/rolldown-with-module-federation-2.0/commits/9ecaa966bbf276a6bd5158cb660b939f087f785a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-09T03:59:04Z","email":"9854+brandonzylstra@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Brandon Zylstra"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-09T03:59:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: fix subject-verb agreement in why-bundlers.md (#8591)\n\nSince \"Deep import chains\" is plural, the verb cannot be conjugated for a singular noun.  (Although conjugation flies under the radar in English, it exists.  Only the third person singular has a different form, normally just with an added \"s\".)\n\nAnother option would be something like \n\n> Using deep import chains also results in network waterfalls\n\nwhere the whole phrase \"using deep import chains\" is now the noun phrase. Since it''s singular (it refers to an action), \"results\" is now the expected conjugation form.\n\nSigned-off-by: Brandon Zylstra <9854+brandonzylstra@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"540fb721fb8f1187c35901184cdcdbe85960a58d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shulaoda/rolldown-with-module-federation-2.0/git/trees/540fb721fb8f1187c35901184cdcdbe85960a58d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shulaoda/rolldown-with-module-federation-2.0/git/commits/9ecaa966bbf276a6bd5158cb660b939f087f785a","verification":{"payload":"tree 540fb721fb8f1187c35901184cdcdbe85960a58d\nparent 8ef88a4e095e451e7b45ce1be6a4898ab6b32610\nauthor Brandon Zylstra <9854+brandonzylstra@users.noreply.github.com> 1773028744 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773028744 +0800\n\ndocs: fix subject-verb agreement in why-bundlers.md (#8591)\n\nSince \"Deep import chains\" is plural, the verb cannot be conjugated for a singular noun.  (Although conjugation flies under the radar in English, it exists.  Only the third person singular has a different form, normally just with an added \"s\".)\n\nAnother option would be something like \n\n> Using deep import chains also results in network waterfalls\n\nwhere the whole phrase \"using deep import chains\" is now the noun phrase. Since it''s singular (it refers to an action), \"results\" is now the expected conjugation form.\n\nSigned-off-by: Brandon Zylstra <9854+brandonzylstra@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJprkWICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqk4QAFLWKdtGdhbFmBJEERAF0ymd\nquJaWdm/TxI6Bc6z0Vb3/4Fp7apSexOkFNmw0zDZzTN8ZabvRaeetm/gGRMFu/X9\njG0kdcg09RD6XI91+ifCBUMTM/s43EqLFceW499Isusg7n4lgDg+MA5SVz/DzOiY\n6Nysd47Vzr3jdhGg1FgXNQoRMZsSeXBrLPPFxALC8wAvSLwrrBT2I0yG/8QdG86y\nPKD5VXmVEyDlnXc29eE4jQggObJiT0HEy6i4rt7Uq9ylWBtluWONxO7qaIrXA3d9\nWS1cbGEOdlMym0NE5Ob3H5vdNcw+SCfjj2bx1EdbQYiiYTeMGgU8ZlRReEIeSKBh\nIwcDlIPTm/jxp8XcgThQ3d5/A9yiMLpJkGzFwahhKhwV9r7aGw2kQvbAxVfX9fK+\nXtJADZ7s44ZdS9y9fFxe6E7T76hGWG5mV6DqnY4OAkuBt5vPZnTe5VOZE8i1pfAq\nzpeY/lAeEcGTBbrTb2b9hA5IFaQDPYGYaKAxjq9hBdMRwpJxLAGMSgSZ0MzYXAxO\nsDlOnPKGT9nV0JbqPC5Y5qGziISj6zmmsn/oF4Bw/V/5Ode6of+Jxm9oyjjMoZAx\nJZG8Sssgl72ardSdFwYomWISYN3glnlVMcSKpCyNppPojK0sbUYbSZiuEMy5V8/b\n2KHIDmekPyFg6eid1zA3\n=xyv/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-10T07:34:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url"